{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker","id":1065343,"title":"Okay, so let's read this thing [Hurt Locker]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-20T11:58:04-07:00","id":1065343,"title":"Okay, so let's read this thing [Hurt Locker]","content":"I'm a complete <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> novice and finished reading the rulebook just last night. You can read my thoughts on that that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1051116-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing\"><b>HERE</b></a>. I've also recently started a play-by-post solo game you can read <a href=\"http://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9w_tLv7Inayalh6S0JIOW5aSUk/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>HERE</b></a>. Now, without any experience, I'm going to jump straight into <b>Hurt Locker</b> (love the name, by the way). My goal with this thread is to present my thoughts as I read through the entire book, and to discuss anything and everything in the book that catches my attention.<br /> <br /> If you didn't read my other thread, I should point out from the beginning. I'm writing this <i>while </i>I'm reading the book and I'm presenting my ideas (and poor jokes) unedited as I go through the book's content. I don't go back to change paragraphs after later revelations and my posts can therefore contradict themselves. If you're wondering what questions I pose and what to reply to, focus on any questions I've posed late in the posts. If I've marked a question with blue text, I want to highlight it especially and create a discussion around it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FICTION: HERO OF WAR by David A Hill Jr</b><br /> <br /> I like the layout of the page here that makes the story look like it's part of a folder. The cursive font is a bit difficult to read though, but I accept it because it fits the layout.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;A kid named after a parent is like tattooing someone's name on you. It's a stupid choice that too many people make.&quot; </i>I wonder if this is an expression of David Hill's own opinions, since he's apparently a &quot;Junior&quot; himself. Since I'm not a native Englisher (as proven by me calling it an <i>Englisher</i>), I'm not part of a culture where naming children after parents is a thing---at all. Unless it's for their middle name. Then it's very common. We don't have an equivalent of &quot;Junior&quot; in Sweden to call someone sharing the name of his father. It seems like a cultural thing that's more common in the US and that I can't really associate with. Paying respect to one's family is usually done through middle names. Does &quot;Junior&quot; dominate the named-after-parent domain in the US, or do you use middle names for that too? My middle name is after my uncle, by the way. I think I'm digressing, but I'm curious.<br /> <br /> Speaking of names, <i>Matthew Randolph Comstock</i> is an awesome one. Man, that letter was a hard read. I'm glad I'm not Mister Comstock. It was good though. You could feel Hannah's emotion throughout. It felt believable. By the way, I'm 100% sure that Mister Comstock isn't going to be able to read this letter. The book is named <b>Hurt Locker</b> after all. The guy's so dead I can smell the rot through the monitor.<br /> <br /> Ooooooh! &lt;--- I just read the part where the revelation is. I was ... <i>kind of but not really right</i>. I liked this <b>much </b>better than what I assumed would be the stereotypical knocking on the door scene with the army guy who the dead soldier saved personally on the field embraces the wailing widow and keeps her from falling to the floor despite the fact that her legs are too weak to carry her.<br /> <br /> <b>Spoiler alert:</b> Mister Comstock is comatose and they take out the plug. It's written that way to highlight the nasty consequences of violence. Had David Hill gone with the scene where the fancy army dude is knocking on the door to tell Hannah that Matthew was killed in an act of heroism, it would have romanticized combat and detracted from the gritty reality that this book wants to present. I haven't read past the introductory fiction yet, but I can tell that much. This book is going to be gritty, nasty, and show you how you'll piss your pants before you die.<br /> <br /> This was a very successful piece of intro fiction, unlike the bad one that introduces the rulebook. Kudos to David Junior.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TABLE OF CONTENTS</b><br /> <br /> So the book will be divided into the following chapters: <i>Introduction</i>, <i>Stories of Violence </i>(seems to be focusing on Storyteller advice which is always welcome), <i>Instruments of Violence </i>(focuses on game mechanical additions to character creation and violence rules), <i>The Other Side </i>(more scary horror fuel), <i>Tokyo </i>(it seems like some kind of suggested setting material), <i>Equipment </i>(more types of weapons and combat-oriented gear) and <i>Conditions </i>(an appendix of additional conditions).<br /> <br /> I'm mainly interested in the <i>Instruments of Violence </i>chapter, but the Tokyo one makes me curious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>INTRODUCTION</b><br /> <br /> The book references <b>Armory </b>and <b>Armory: Reloaded</b>, none of which I have read or even heard about.<br /> <br /> I've read what the book is about, and I'm sold. I've read what the book is not about, and I'm still sold. I like that it presents violence as a gritty and real thing without getting political about it.<br /> <br /> I don't intend to make my first chronicle about violence. I intend to have some violent scenes, but it's definitely not a focus. My focus is more of a creepy mystery. However, when violence happens, I want it to have impact. I want my player to be afraid.<br /> <br /> The book addresses some balance concerns for player characters using other splats, like Vampires. I don't know anything about how Vampires play yet, and I appreciate the tip because of that.<br /> <br /> <br /> This will have to be enough of a starting post so far. Next time I'll get into <b>Chapter One: Stories of Violence</b>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T12:24:25-07:00","id":1065358,"title":"","content":"So, my dad was raised Catholic and has four names - his first, middle, confirmation, and last name. My first, middle, and last are the same as his middle, confirmation, and last. My middle name (my dad's confirmation name) is also the same as the first name of one of his many brothers, and this brother also took my dad's first name as his confirmation name. Another of his brothers has a middle name that starts with the same letter as mine, but due to a typo on his birth cirtificut, starts with a lower-case letter. My middle name intentionally starts with a lower case letter in reference to this. My mom's family had the tradition of naming all the firstborn male children William, and if I'd had a brother my parents would have named him that, and given him my mom's last name (which she kept when she married my dad). But, that didn't happen. If I ever have a son I would like to name him William, but I don't see that happening in the foreseeable future.<br /> <br /> I've always found all of my family references in my name to be really cool, personally. Too bad they're typically-male names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-20-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T12:29:26-07:00","id":1065364,"title":"","content":"I'm going to try and read this one with you. I've skimmed Hurt Locker, and focused on Tokyo, but I haven't had time to read the entire book in depth yet. In fact, I hadn't read the opening fiction either, though i did before I read you post. Youch! That is one effective piece of fiction. I like how it doesn't feature the supernatural at all, which emphasizes just how fucked up people can be as a baseline before supernatural shenanigans enter the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T12:34:25-07:00","id":1065368,"title":"","content":"You might want to either tag David so he gets a notification or share it with him on twitter or other social media. I assume he enjoys positive commentary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T12:51:44-07:00","id":1065374,"title":"","content":"If you want to amplify aspects of horror and helplessness in a game which is essentially fantasy, considering the cadre of characters, violence is an excellent option. Grisly scenes can highlight an enemy, and make a player more interested and engaged in their investigations. Furthermore, hints of violence used as a contrasting agent (blood across a blackboard, a gentle stigmatic family member with a malfunction suddenly acting in pain, agony, and fear) can further invest a character/player in uncovering sickening, paradigm-shifting truths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T15:49:02-07:00","id":1065459,"title":"","content":"I'm a reverse Junior. I'm named after my father but not in the same order. Dad's first name is my middle name. Dad's middle name is my first name. Since I was a small smart aleck everytime Dad says I'm doing something backwards I say it's all his fault for naming me thusly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T16:32:49-07:00","id":1065479,"title":"","content":"My mum was named after my grandmother, until she married my dad and took his last name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T17:34:10-07:00","id":1065516,"title":"","content":"Well, my mother's family is Jewish, and you're not allowed to name your kids after living relatives in Judaism, only dead ones. So that holds true for both sides of my family. My family all is middle names for that though. I do have a friend who's family has an interesting tradition, ever generation they alternate first and last names. So his name is, as an example, John Abraham, and his father is Abraham John, and his grandfather is John Abraham, and so on. Interesting little tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T17:44:15-07:00","id":1065519,"title":"","content":"Huh. I thought that was just a tradition in some jewish groups and not an actual rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T18:30:43-07:00","id":1065536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1065519#post1065519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I thought that was just a tradition in some jewish groups and not an actual rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Definitely more of a tradition. When it's a dead relatives name though, it's supposed to help keep the in living memory in some way for as long as possibleI'm named after two great-uncles myself, for both my first and middle name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 03-20-2017, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T19:34:50-07:00","id":1065549,"title":"","content":"Ah, my family are of the atheist-socialist type of American Jew, so I never really got much of an education in Judaism, so many things I think are rules turn out to be merely tradition and vice versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T03:45:37-07:00","id":1065654,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>CHAPTER ONE: STORIES OF VIOLENCE</b></span><br /> <br /> I have no experience watsoever with the violence mechanics in game. I haven't gotten that far yet in my storytelling of <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>. I did re-read the paragraphs about violence in the rulebook yesterday to see if I can better grasp the new information added in this book. I think I have a fairly solid idea of how violence works in game now, though I admit I'd have to look at notes to remind myself of the nitty and gritty.<br /> <br /> This chapter addresses storytelling violence and the first thing it does is to remind the reader that immersion comes from narration. With a decade of <b>Exalted</b> experience, I've done my fair share of narrative stunts, and I even try to add those details to less story-intensive games, like <b>Dungeons and Dragons</b>. To show and not tell is the 101 of impactful storytelling in any medium. Some of my friends like shocking descriptions of violence for heightened tension (interesting fact is that the one who likes the most shocking descriptions in game is also the one who is the most queasy when it comes to violent movies) and others are at least tolerant to it. I don't try to make every attack into a finishing move in Mortal Kombat, but I do tune the descriptions up towards the gory more often than not. I still want it to be believable though. Too much often becomes silly.<br /> <br /> I 100% agree with the mention of chronicles being about individuals, and that &quot;evil&quot; or &quot;good&quot; characters rob people from exploring variables. I try (and sometimes succeed---sometimes fail) to keep this in mind even when I roleplay &quot;supernatural evils.&quot; I've had Abyssal campaigns for Exalted where even Deathlords have expressed mercy, and empathy, because though they are seen as evil and their atrocities have been considered evil, their driving forces have not necessarily been so.<br /> <br /> The chapter goes on to discuss the impact of violence in other related gamelines. Since I'm not familiar with those yet but I've already decided to read <b>Vampire: The Requiem </b>next, I'm curious to see the differences. Actually, what interests me most when reading this is the information on all of the other splats. It shows how little I know about this when I see the word <i>Uratha </i>and realized I had probably never encountered it before. And yet the premium Werewolf book is right there on my couch next to me. It's getting all the more compelling now, but I'll still read Vampire first. Mages seem absolutely terrifying and limitless. I haven't played Mage, but I think they could be scary villains for games where you play other splats. I still can't really wrap my head around Prometheans. I see Frankenstein's Monster and I see Exalted's Liminal Exalted, but something tells me that I still don't really see Prometheans. The paragraph(s) about Changeling is the longest and most substantial, probably because David Hill used to develop Changeling. It doesn't give enough information to actually tell me what Changelings are, but neither is that the intent of the paragraph. It's written for those already familiar with these splats.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>OPTIONAL SYSTEM: INTEGRITY BY ATTRITION</b><br /> <br /> This presents a system replacing the standard Integrity loss rules with an attrition-based system using <i>counters. </i>Your Integrity track has three unfilled dots which will be the counters you need to threaten Integrity. <i>So far, I have no idea what is meant by this.</i><br /> <br /> When the player's character participates in violent/traumatic scenes, I (as the Storyteller) hands him a counter. I do the same whenever he'd face a breaking point. Whenever he gets a counter, he also gets a Beat. Once these counters fill the Integrity track, the player gives back the counters to the Storyteller and reduces his Integrity by one. <i>I get it. </i><br /> <br /> The counters owned by the player acts as a penalty to Empathy, Socialize and other rolls reflecting the character's ability to relate to other people. So when he holds two counters, he's at -2 to all those rolls. Once he gets the third counter and finally breaks, he can act without a penalty again but his Integrity has been eroded.<br /> <br /> The character can shed counters by positive experiences. Once all counters are gone, another positive experience could potentially bring back a dot of Integrity.<br /> <br /> This is an interesting system. It didn't explicitly say so, but I <i>assume </i>that each time the Storyteller would hand out a counter corresponds to a <i>breaking point </i>using the core system. The rolls are made like normal, but the counter is handed out alongside whatever condition the character may have gained from the experience. Correct me if I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> There are two new Merits associated with the <i>Integrity by Attrition </i>rule. One of them lets you shed the social penalty for a scene in exchange for a Condition. The other Merit lets you swap out using your unfilled Integrity dots for your combined (Resolve + Composure) dots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FRAMING SCENES</b><br /> <br /> The book gives some solid advice on how to portray mechanical advantages and disadvantages through the scene. This is something very valuable to me as a new Storyteller since I have issues with figuring out what bonuses and penalties to give my player's character.<br /> <br /> I don't have that much to say about this other than that it's solid advice for me who is new to the system. I'd even go so far as to say that people thinking about picking up the rulebook should also pick up Hurt Locker as a package deal.<br /> <br /> The book goes on to give a large number of example scenes presented using this system, with listed <i>advantages</i>, <i>penalties</i> and <i>dramatic failures</i>. It encourages me as a Storyteller to start listing potential scenes like that as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>VIOLENCE GROUPS</b><br /> <br /> Barring mental illness, people aren't violent without reason. The book takes a lot of space to explain the mentality behind violence, and how &quot;sane people&quot; need Aspirations to be their driving force behind violent deeds. Without such driving forces, inflicting harm shouldn't come easy.<br /> <br /> I think this is important to keep in mind for believable storytelling. It's often forgotten in roleplaying games, mostly so in fantasy games, where heroes strike down a hundred bandits and then have a beer afterwards, not even feeling the slightest remorse over a single one of those kills. I enjoy when violence has emotional impact even in such games. I like the show Critical Role, not because of any particular fondness for Dungeons and Dragons (I do play it sometimes), but because the actors involved are all roleplayers who enjoy emotional and narrative depth to their story. If you can add emotional impact to a game like Dungeons and Dragons, then you're a good roleplayer. If you can't even do that to a narrative-game like Chronicles of Darkness, then you're going to lose out on the experience.<br /> <br /> The books describes how to build a group, organization or violent mob where you basically averages traits for the whole group. I wonder if there are group sheets as well, sort of like character sheets. There's a new Merit called <i>Organization Size </i>that you can take when part of a violence group.<br /> <br /> I haven't commented too much on the very substantial information about violence groups. Some paragraphs were a little too substantial to retain interest, but it's been very valuable as a whole. For when I want to bring organizations into my game, I have here a serious source to look into for helpful information.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to continue with <b>Chapter Two: Instruments of Violence </b>for the next post. Anything I've addressed above is open for discussion, but I'd like to mainly bring up the <i>Integrity by Attrition </i>optional system. Do you use that system in place of the standard one? How do you like it? What don't you like about it? Should I use it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T06:55:35-07:00","id":1065726,"title":"","content":"I've used something similar to the IbA system before, and it's worked rather well. I handed out the tokens at places of stress/duress (breaking point triggers), and only made the players roll to decrease Morality (Integrity) when they'd gotten four. Using that system, coupled with the Forbidden Lore alternate concepts, was an interesting take on human functionality in extreme situations.<br /> <br /> I'm still partial to the Unknown Armies stress system.<br /> <br /> I think there's three points to make. First, I enjoy seeing a published, streamlined version of the system I hacked together. Second, I don't think you should switch to too many alternate systems if you or your player is just getting acquainted with the rules. Third, I think that if you see a rule you like, use it: whether or not people agree with you, and whether or not you feel the need to adjust things to fit, or even if you want to plug-in a concept from outside WoD/CoD, you are the one framing the story your players tell. If you like <i>Integrity by Attrition</i>, I say go for it. I don't think it's inherently better or worse than any of the other alternates.<br /> <br /> <br /> I thoroughly agree with you about how useful this book is, for concepts and hard mechanics. One of my favourite additions to the game stock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:23:22-07:00","id":1065746,"title":"","content":"You seem very curious about the supernatural gamelines, would you be interested in a brief summary of what they're each about? Or do you prefer to remain as unspoiled about them as possible until you're ready to read them yourself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:25:14-07:00","id":1065747,"title":"","content":"I think Integrity by Attrition works for a particular kind of gameplay atmosphere. Using the roll for Integrity Breaking Points, if you can keep your head, if you have the fortitude represented by Resolve + Composure, if you use the centring techniques of the Meditative Mind Merit, you can shake off the trauma and keep moving forwards. That suits an atmosphere where tenacity and force of will are the things that keep humans alive in a harsh world.<br /> <br /> The Integrity by Attrition system, on the other hand, works if you're telling a story where it is important to show the toll trauma takes on a person and their relationships. No matter how strong your willpower (Resolve + Composure) trauma takes a toll, but the more used to the hurt you are (lower Integrity) the harder you need to be pushed to break. But each counter is a penalty to Social Actions (except Intimidation, is the way I've run it), meaning the strain of keeping it together is getting to you, and you find yourself removed further from other people until you break and find a new plateau to sit on. The other side of Integrity by Attrition, though, I absolutely love, because I like (for the most part) doing away with paying Experience to restore Integrity Traits. It's also the reason, I think, the subsystem is under the section <b>Stories About Moving On</b>. Positive interactions with people <i>remove Breaking Point Counters</i>. You go to people in your support network, and you reach out for help, and it helps you <i>heal</i>. Seek help often enough, and you start to get <i>better</i> if you have the Willpower (Resolve + Composure) to accept your new sense of self.<br /> <br /> The two Merits attached to it are also pretty good (Smile Through It suggests to me that in a strict reading of Integrity by Attrition you get a Beat per Breaking Point Counter in lieu of the normal Condition, and the Merit lets you get the Condition more or less on demand to force relatively normal social interaction) and help enforce that mood. You can, through force of will, endure a little more, fake normalcy, but if you don't get help, eventually it will get worse. It's very humanizing, and I personally like it, though it might not be the best system for a group of relatively isolated PCs who don't have people they can (or would even want to) go and talk to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T07:30:15-07:00","id":1065750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1065654#post1065654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>VIOLENCE GROUPS</b><br /> The books describes how to build a group, organization or violent mob where you basically averages traits for the whole group. I wonder if there are group sheets as well, sort of like character sheets. There's a new Merit called <i>Organization Size </i>that you can take when part of a violence group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I proposed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021570-hurt-locker-violence-groups-sheets\">my Violence Groups sheets ideas</a> for <b>Mr Gone</b>, but he doesn't seem to posted ended version. I will ask him about it, and probably he will link sheets in the topic linked by me when it's done ( as most of time he do this after my sheets ideas ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-21-2017, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:24:03-07:00","id":1065887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1065746#post1065746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem very curious about the supernatural gamelines, would you be interested in a brief summary of what they're each about? Or do you prefer to remain as unspoiled about them as possible until you're ready to read them yourself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to summarize them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:39:14-07:00","id":1065917,"title":"","content":"I generally prefer normal Integrity (esp. since it's easier to deal with non-normal people). However I love the idea of Integrity by Attrition for shorter games (like convention games and the like) because it makes Integrity much more immediate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:46:07-07:00","id":1065922,"title":"","content":"Another problem with Integrity by Attrition is how large the dice penalty can become for a low Integrity character. That really makes it unfitting for longer games where the character's can approach the bottom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:47:52-07:00","id":1065924,"title":"","content":"hmm, interesting. A few of you are saying that Integrity by Attrition is more immediate, but it seems like it would actually take longer to lose Integrity this way as you get three-four 'extra lives' before you lose it. Am I reading this wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:50:20-07:00","id":1065926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1065887#post1065887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feel free to summarize them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also have a synopsis on the various gamelines for friends of mine who express interests in the game. It's written from a more jokey perspective though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T13:59:05-07:00","id":1065930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1065924#post1065924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm, interesting. A few of you are saying that Integrity by Attrition is more immediate, but it seems like it would actually take longer to lose Integrity this way as you get three-four 'extra lives' before you lose it. Am I reading this wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Heavy Arms meant immediate as in it has a very tangible effect even after short play. Not that your Integrity would fall faster.<br /> Curiously IbA would probably make you fall faster at high Integrity but a lot slower at low Integrity while the original rules gives you a bonus to breaking point checks if you have high Integrity, and a penalty if you have low Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:30:21-07:00","id":1065986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1065750#post1065750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I proposed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021570-hurt-locker-violence-groups-sheets\">my Violence Groups sheets ideas</a> for <b>Mr Gone</b>, but he doesn't seem to posted ended version. I will ask him about it, and probably he will link sheets in the topic linked by me when it's done ( as most of time he do this after my sheets ideas ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, sorry...guess I dropped the ball and got side tracked or something.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll try to start on em soon...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:57:35-07:00","id":1066009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1065887#post1065887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feel free to summarize them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, this turned out to be much harder than I thought it would be, and I'm not 100% sure if I'm emphasizing the right parts. Kind of hard to know from an inside perspective what's going to be the best way to present it to someone with an outside perspective. But, here goes nothing.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b> puts the players in the role the Kindred \u2013 vampires from one of five lines of descent, known as Clans, each based on an iconic vampire archetype. A strong focus of Requiem is the gradual descent into monstrosity as the character loses touch with the human experience - young vampires try to cling to who they were in life, while elders become jaded and callous. Running parallel to the lamentation of lost humanity, however, is the reverie in eternal life, youth, and power. To this end, the Kindred organize themselves into Covenants \u2013 social, political, and ideological organizations. If a character\u2019s Clan answers the existential question, <i>what have I become?</i> then their Covenant answers the question, <i>and what do I do now?</i> There is frequently a great deal of political maneuvering in vampire games \u2013 vying for power, influence, and territory. As would be expected when you take a bunch of blood-thirsty monsters trying desperately to keep up the fa\u00e7ade of humanity, throw them all in the same small geographical area, and force them to pretend to get along.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> is perhaps a little less straightforward than Requiem. You can certainly play the iconic Wolfman story if you want, but the central focus of the game is a bit further afield of that archetype. The Uratha \u2013 the name the protagonist faction of werewolves uses for themselves \u2013 are beings torn between flesh and spirit. There is a heavy focus on interaction with the spirit world, which you\u2019ve seen a taste of in the CofD core book. Where vampires start out human and degenerate over time into blood-sucking monsters, werewolves are constantly striving for balance between their dual natures. This struggle for Harmony is best expressed by the line\u2019s unofficial catchphrase, <i>The Wolf Must Hunt</i>. As a creature of the Shadow, a werewolf is bound by its nature, and the nature of a wolf is to hunt. Deny this nature, and you end up like Lon Cheney Jr.'s Larry Talbot, a tragic figure who loses control and becomes a slavering beast when the moon is right. Embrace it to the exclusion of your human nature, and you become no different than a spirit, driven by instinct alone. The only way to find Harmony is to honor both sides.<br /> <br /> Where vampires have Clans, werewolves have Auspices \u2013 affinities for a particular phase of the moon. Of course, everyone is familiar with the Full Moon\u2019s warriors, but each of the five phases (full, gibbous, half, crescent, and new) has its favored agents, which can be thought of as answering the question, <i>how do you hunt?</i> Where vampires have Covenants, werewolves have Tribes \u2013 organizations based on a shared sacred prey, answering the question, <i>what do you hunt?</i> While any werewolf may actually hunt any prey, each Tribe has one particular type of prey that they consider most worthy of the Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> is a game of cosmic power and calamitous hubris. Where most other game lines cast the players unambiguously as monsters and forces them to find a way to deal with that, Mage hands the players all the tools they need to make themselves monsters and lets them find the way there on their own. In fact, it\u2019s a point of frequent and very heated debate among the Mage fandom if Mages are even monsters at all, though pretty much everyone can at least agree that they certainly have the potential to be monstrous.<br /> <br /> If Werewolf\u2019s catchphrase is <i>The Wolf Must Hunt</i>, then Mage\u2019s is <i>Addicted to Mystery</i>. The Awakening alluded to in the title is a sort of gnostic revelation that ignites the latent magical potential within every human soul. The Awakened get a glimpse beyond the great Lie, and they are forevermore driven to seek further truth. The setup is often compared to The Matrix, and unsurprisingly so, as both draw heavily from Gnostic philosophy and Plato\u2019s Allegory of the Cave. To think of Mage characters as like Neo would not be <i>too</i> far off the mark, though it is definitely not a perfect analogy.<br /> <br /> Mages Awaken to one of five Paths, which roughly equate to what aspect of reality their revelation allowed them to see beyond, which informs what sort of magic they can most (and least) easily master. They organize themselves within Orders, secret societies of other like-minded mages. Four of these Orders, known as the Diamond, model themselves after a society of Awakened from a mythical Time Before, which they say was erased from the timeline. A fifth is more interested in the here and now, preferring to emulate the magical practices of human cultures from <i>this </i>timeline. Together, these five form the protagonist faction, known collectively as the Pentacle. Another, antagonistic Order, serves the Exarchs - the leaders of the mythical Awakened society, whose hubris was what caused the erasure of their civilization from history (not unlike the Tevinter magisters from the Dragon Age series, if you\u2019re at all familiar).<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean: the Created</b> turns the \u201chuman becomes a monster\u201d formula of most CofD lines on its head. The Created are artificial beings a-la Frankenstein\u2019s monster, assembled from deceased human tissue (and sometimes inanimate matter) and given life by a spark of Divine Fire. But the fire within them is too hot for this mortal world, and burns anyone and everything that gets too close; metaphysically speaking, of course. They don\u2019t literally set things on fire (usually), but they do ignite the passions of those around them. Living, and even undead creatures are inexplicably repulsed by Prometheans, and the longer they spend around others, the worse this gets. If the Divine Fire builds up too much within one place, it can even cause natural disasters. However, the fire also drives the Created to refine themselves, to take their artificial soul and transmute it, as if by the same alchemy that brought them into being, into a true, human soul.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Promethean is a Pinocchio story. It\u2019s about forming an identity, and in so doing, ridding yourself of the turmoil that has plagued you since your creation. There is some controversy surrounding this game, and in particular its overt themes of humanism, where becoming a totally ordinary, mortal, fragile, unpowered human is treated as a desirable goal. Personally I love it, but it\u2019s definitely not for everyone, and it\u2019s not afraid to be the best it can be for those it is, even if that comes at the expense of those for whom it is not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have a rehearsal to be at, but if you like these, I would be happy to do Demon and Changeling as well. Beast and Mummy I'll leave to someone who has actually read the books, and Hunter and Geist I'd prefer to wait until we know more about their upcoming Second Editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-21-2017, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T19:12:15-07:00","id":1066093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1065930#post1065930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Heavy Arms meant immediate as in it has a very tangible effect even after short play. Not that your Integrity would fall faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I meant exactly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066009#post1066009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deny this nature, and you end up like Lon Cheney,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the pet peeve nitpick:<br /> <br /> You end up like Larry Talbot (the character in question).<br /> <br /> Lon Chaney Jr. was clearly a Changeling (I actually don't like doing the whole &quot;What would real world famous person be in the CofD&quot; game, but it was worth it for both to keep the nitpick light, and I find Chaney's life story extremely interesting for someone so remembered for the characters he played).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T20:01:34-07:00","id":1066102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066093#post1066093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the pet peeve nitpick:<br /> <br /> You end up like Larry Talbot (the character in question).<br /> <br /> Lon Chaney Jr. was clearly a Changeling (I actually don't like doing the whole &quot;What would real world famous person be in the CofD&quot; game, but it was worth it for both to keep the nitpick light, and I find Chaney's life story extremely interesting for someone so remembered for the characters he played).</div> </div> </div> </div>No apologies necessary, I appreciate the clarification. I had forgotten the character's name and thought the actor's name would be more recognizable to most anyway. I will edit the post accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T00:58:52-07:00","id":1066170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066009#post1066009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Beast</b> and Mummy I'll leave to someone who has actually read the books,</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'll give it a shot:<br /> <br /> <b>Beast: the Primordial</b>, is a game of Endless Hunger, and is the most recent of the released CofD gamelines (as of this post, Deviant: the Renegades has not been released yet). You play as Beasts, otherwise known as Begotten. They are humans whose souls have been replaced by the souls of archetypal monsters of myth (creatures like dragons, minotaurs, giants, kraken, etc) called a Horror. The source of their powers and their place of origin is the Primordial Dream, a separate dimension where the nightmares of humanity are created and made real. The Beasts believe they are descended from the Dark Mother, a god-like entity that is believed to be the creator of all nightmares, a queen of all monsters (compared to being Lillith, Echidna, Tiamat, etc). Whether she created the Primordial Dream or was simply the first to find it, no one knows for sure.<br /> <br /> Beasts have to sate their hunger by feeding upon humanity's fears. Doing so sates their Horror and keeps it from rampaging. Now feeding does not necessarily have to be actually killing anyone. Depending upon your Hunger, it can be something figurative or metaphorical like winning at a competition or injuring someone in a non-fatal way. Family defines &quot;what kind of monster are you?&quot; (including things like creatures that are massive figuratively or literally, creatures that stalk from the dark, or while Hunger is &quot;how do you feed?&quot; ranging from through punishing others, hoarding something of value, or destroying something of value.<br /> <br /> One of the big obstacles that face all Beasts are Heroes. This is where the game takes it into a direction of subverting the monomyth, the classic &quot;knight vs the dragon&quot; story. Heroes are people that are affected by the Beasts' Nightmares and have glimpsed the Primordial Dream. Doing so unbalances them to where they become obsessed with the Beasts. Specifically that Beasts represent something WRONG. Something that only the Hero believes that they can take down. And they will do anything to do that, even if it means harming others around them, because it's all worth it in the end when the Beast is lying dead on the floor.<br /> <br /> (and no, Heroes are NOT the same as Hunters from Hunter: the Vigil. book is very clear about that)<br /> <br /> This line is notable for being designed from the beginning on being crossover friendly. Beasts believe that all the supernatural splats are distantly descended from the Dark Mother. As such, they feel bonds of Kinship towards the other supernaturals, or they do what they can to forge Kinship bonds. While the other splats do not necessarily reciprocate those feelings of Kinship, they are at the very least not initially hostile towards the Begotten. Curiously, they do not have Kinship with Demons from Demon: the Descent...mostly due to how the Beasts are pretty sure the God Machine and all of its' creations are NOT of the Dark Mother's creation.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Unfortunately the thing about Beast is that it's the most...controversial of all the CofD lines.<br /> <br /> When it was initially pitched to Kickstarter, OPP put up a rough draft of the core rulebook as part of it. When people read it. the response was...less-then-warm, to put it lightly. People felt that the game was aimless in that Feeding as the only drive and motivation for Beasts wasn't very interesting. Heroes were seen as too sympathetic, to the point that people were wondering why they weren't playing as Heroes instead. So the developers had to scramble to rewrite the text. This included things like making Heroes unambiguously assholes (although this was somewhat stepped back with the Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes book), the method of how humans become Beasts are changed (from the previous Homecoming where the Beast was always one they just need to accept their birthright, to the Devouring where the Horror is an independent entity that consumes their soul and becomes their host/victim), stuff like that.<br /> <br /> One of the big changes was to add in &quot;lessons&quot;. Where Beasts feel that as humanity has progressed, they've grown arrogant and ignorant of the world around them. That they've become too reliant and complacent on the advantages of technology and progress. So, they feel that they need to remind people about all the bad things in the world and to take things seriously...by being those bad things. By terrifying them to make them realize those dangers of the world.<br /> <br /> This in particular has been a big point of contention for people. Since a.) we have a group of people forcing their beliefs on someone else, usually against their will b.) there is no mechanics supporting or reinforcing these Lessons c.) there's inconsistencies in the text on how Beasts feel about Lessons. That it seems to be the singular reason given on why Beasts Feed...but at the same time it's also stated that Beasts know full well that their Horrors don't care about giving Lessons and that all that matters is that they Feed.<br /> <br /> Which has created...mixed messaging on what the main theme of Beast is.<br /> <br /> Even then, in both the KS version and the final version, there is no getting around that the Beast's existence predicates on them hurting people. Either physically, mentally, or emotionally, they HAVE to hurt other people. Because if they don't, they will die. And, well, I don't think I need to explain how that could be seen as a problem to anyone.<br /> <br /> And on a technical level, you can tell that there are places where the text hasn't been adjusted to fit the revised text. So that...hasn't helped either.<br /> <br /> So, Beast the Primordial is the most polarizing gameline of CofD at best, the absolute weakest of the CofD gameline at worst.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> For me, I see Beast as a game of compromised morality.<br /> <br /> It's a game that asks you &quot;how far will you go to achieve the greater good?&quot; The greater good either for society as a whole, or for yourself on defining and reaching your Are you someone that's trying to do good by doing horrible things? Or are you someone who is a horrible person but trying to justify what you are doing as being, in the long run, good? Beasts have to do horrible things just so they can live. Heroes believe that they are doing the right thing by slaying the evil Beast, and that every horrible thing they do can be forgiven for doing so.<br /> <br /> It takes the most essential tool in storytelling, the &quot;protagonist vs antagonist&quot; conflict, turns it on its head, and ask &quot;is it REALLY that straightforward to believe that the protagonist is Right and the antagonist is Wrong? Or is there far more to it?&quot;<br /> <br /> That said...I understand why people wouldn't click with this. I understand that anything that messes with morality and playing with someone's perception of Right and Wrong is not only difficult to do, but is something that people are not going to take kindly to. Especially if they feel the game makes broad, over-generalized, absolute statements about what's really Right and Wrong. I understand player's desires to play generally good characters and who have more control of said characters so they can perform good actions, and not be held back by the games' mechanics. I understand that the fact Beasts are required to hurt people is something people cannot forgive, no matter what the reasons Beasts come up with to justify their behavior. Or, worst case, the behavior that Beasts exhibit to their victims just hits too close to home for people and reminds them of real-life experiences they'd rather not remember.<br /> <br /> Either way, it's honestly up to you decide how you feel about the book. When you are able to, give the book a read through, and decide for yourself how to feel about the game. And if you do decide to run a game of Beast, you absolutely HAVE to talk to your players about it if they are new to Beast. Yes, considering the mature themes that the CofD gameline(s) covers that's a no brainer, but for Beast I'd say this is a requirement. The game's content is NOT for everyone, and has to be discussed with players to see if not only are they comfortable with the game, as well as clearly dictate the main intent and theming for the chronicle you'd be running.<br /> <br /> ...now if you'll excuse me, imma make like Smaug and go into a long deep sleep, and when I wake up go back to my semi-regular lurking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-22-2017, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T03:39:28-07:00","id":1066220,"title":"","content":"More on Beast:<br /> <br /> Remember how people say you're the protagonist of your own story? You grow up, meet people, embark on a quest, slay the monster and win the prize. Even villains have their own stories, unorthodox as their idea of quest and prize may be. We sometimes star as the supporting cast or even side characters of someone else's story, but we still have our own to continue. We all live our own story.<br /> <br /> Except you.<br /> <br /> When you surrendered yourself to nightmares from Primordial times, knowingly or not, the nightmare became a Horror that Devoured your human soul. And with that went away your story, replaced by a Primordial one that has rung true through the ages. Now, you are the archetypical monster in legends and mythologies that some anthropologists identify as common cultural constructs designed to explain how the world works and how humans should behave within it through the medium of fearful warnings. What archetype you and your Horror belong to is your Family, and your Family shares the common experience of being feared in certain ways.<br /> <br /> Of course, many Beasts still want to carry on a human life, despite knowing literally on a soul-deep level that they are no longer human. However a Hunger gnaws inside you, driving you to do things that only a monster would. Deny your Hunger too long, and your Horror slowly leaks out to the physical world, moving you further away from humanity. Ironically enough, to be human you must be a monster.<br /> <br /> Although some Beasts revel in their newfound monstrosity, and some Beasts deny it with all their heart, many reach a point of compromise where they conclude that if they must be a monster, they'll do it on their own terms. See the above bit on anthropolgy and monsters; the Beast decides that the least she can do is choosing the lessons her actions teach to the people, contributing to human society in ways only a monster can. And most often, the only way a monster can.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, you are not alone in the existential angst of losing your humanity to become the Other, the antagonist of everyone's stories. Not only there are your fellow Beasts, there are monsters hiding in the darkness who are not stories made real but realities making stories. You tap into your resonance with the footsteps these monsters leave in the collective Dream of humanity, establishing Kinship with them. They may not like you, or even know you, but you still welcome them into the extended family of monsters and legends.<br /> <br /> Even still, some Beasts seek a way out of the narrative they're forced into, the Monomyth they're dancing in. They seek to become once again the main character of your own story instead of the conflict-to-overcome of eveyone else's stories. Those who succeed in this endeavor find themselves Inheriting the legacy of the Dark Mother, the progenitor of monsters. Whether by Merging your flesh with your soul, Retreating into the deep Dreams, or Incarnating the novel story starring a monster as the protagonist that you wrote yourself, the Inheritance is there to be claimed by those who are worthy of it.<br /> <br /> But wait, if the monsters of legends are made real, then what about the heroes of legend? Yes, the Heroes exist, chosen by the same Primordial Dream that chooses the monsters. Unlike Beasts, however, they suffer no angst from being denied their place as the protagonist. In fact, it's the opposite, where the world seemingly designates them as 'the' protagonist. Those who are firm in character and clear of perspective can see through the white noise of a millenia of Dreams, and successfully glean wisdom from the Horrors of the world so that they can dispel the fears suffered by the people. Those who are unsure of their place in the world, or overwhelmed by what the world throws at them, are consumed by the Dream and become little more than characters in fiction who only exist to express the Monomyth in the most blatant ways possible. Here, 'blatant ways' mean &quot;Kill the monsters and its minions&quot; and &quot;Everyone else is a sidekick in my story.&quot; Unfortunately, since becoming a Hero is facilitated by a traumatizing contact with the Primordial Dream, the latter are more common in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  added some sentences 03-22-2017, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T04:10:06-07:00","id":1066228,"title":"","content":"On <b>Demon the Descent</b>:<br /> <br /> Imagine that you are an angel of God. You do as your Creator says, confident in your place in the world and blissful in your communion with the Divine. You are the one working behind the scenes of the world, turning its wheels and lubricating its gears so that the providence of God play out in a universal harmony. Then doubts creep into your heart, as if it were clockwork creaking. Perhaps you found yourself in love with humans and their work, and loathed to see it perish. Perhaps you found yourself hollow and empty, as what you nurtured and cared for were sacrificed in the greater good. Perhaps you found yourself just another piece to be used and replaced, and you said no. Perhaps you came to see something was not going right, and lost faith in the mysterious ways of God. Or perhaps you concluded that what you were seeing was just plain <i>wrong</i>.<br /> <br /> In that moment, you were torn apart from your grace and Fell. From that moment, you were Unchained from God, whom you realize was not a benevolent parent or a wise lord but a cold, distant Machine. Your angelic Corpus has been shattered, but you still retain the design of the God-Machine in your broken hardware and It's programming in your frustrated software. Thus you belong to an Incarnation of your inception, a reminder of the luminous being you were.<br /> <br /> However, the God-Machine does not so easily give up on It's rogue agents. It leaves them be if It deems them inconsequential to Its purpose, but sooner or later the fallen angels cross Its designs and Infrastructure placed across the world. And the God-Machine's infrastructure is indeed placed across the whole world, for It is the King of This World. For this the Unchained seek a Descent into Hell, where they can be truly free from God's cold light. Demons being highly individual creatures from moment of their birth, they all have different ideas on Hell. Nevertheless, broad strokes of philosophy on how to achieve their Descent and common motives for their Falls group demons into Agendas and agencies.<br /> <br /> Because God is not above in some far heaven but right here in this world, demons put top priority on hiding from It's eyes and hands, manifesting as angels and cultists. Fortunately, all demons embezzle the divine underpinnings of reality that supported their angelic existence, and weave it into a Cover. Stay under Cover, and the God-Machine will see the demon as just another human, just another humber. Compromise the Cover, and the God-Machine starts to compute the expected utility of sending agents to retrieve Its assets. Fortunately, demons may hack into and reroute the same occult formulae the Machine uses to place Its angels on Earth, bulwarking their Cover. The most common way to achieve this is to sign Pacts with humans, granting them favors in return for fragments of their lives, or sometimes ejecting a human's soul and wholly taking his place in the world. For this, even the most callous and misanthropic of demons sing and dance with humans and take part in all their wants and needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  typo 03-22-2017, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T04:12:24-07:00","id":1066230,"title":"","content":"The best argument I've seen for Beast is that in many ways it's going back to the idea that kicked off this entire franchise.<br /> <br /> &quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, you have to hurt people to live, what's new about that? The trick is to do it in a way that causes minimum harm (or just target the assholes who deserve it, there's enough to go around) and maybe gives something back in return, and then use your powers to do some good in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T04:39:01-07:00","id":1066237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066230#post1066230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best argument I've seen for Beast is that in many ways it's going back to the idea that kicked off this entire franchise.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, you have to hurt people to live, what's new about that? The trick is to do it in a way that causes minimum harm (or just target the assholes who deserve it, there's enough to go around) and maybe gives something back in return, and then use your powers to do some good in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I really don't think Beast's &quot;you have to hurt people to live&quot; is all that new for CofD. Vampires have to drink human blood, werewolves have to hunt, etc. Nor is their justification of their own behavior an unusual thing. I think what bugs some folks about it is that Beast has stripped away some of the layers of metaphor, making it too real for some folks' comfort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T06:38:01-07:00","id":1066274,"title":"","content":"Well, its also no small part in that the hurting is differently from vampire, werewolf or changeling. Vampire blood dolls can be compared to a blood donor at Red Cross, and the feeding can take any form from mystical rite to sex to loyalty. And it feels good for all involved. Werewolves... well, eating humans is actually rare; most hunts against humans don't involve death and injury, and even when it does, the suffering is over quickly. Changelings snack on willpower, something that is so ephemeral you might not even realize it, through any kind of emotions. Sex, sports, and working in funeral homes are all valid and pretty harmless ways of feeding. Hells, I have Enchanting Performance on my current 'ling, and he can basically give out Inspired at will. Take glamour from lots of people, they all lose one point of willpower, but they get it back from Inspired, ending up in a net gain of glamour for the changeling and no loss for the humans. Demons have people willingly sign the dotted line, and neither mages nor prommies feed off people at all.<br /> <br /> Beasts feed on suffering and pain and loss. They're naturally sadistic, and the nature of that sadistic Hunger makes it hard to figure out ways to balance it out with some kind of positive event. You have to make people -hurt-. Not just physically, but on an emotional level, which, by many, is considered far worse than just a physical hurt you might not even feel. Beasts want to pull people off the hill and enjoy the thrill of their loss. In a very real way, its a game about indulging sadism, and that's not something many people are comfortable doing. Hells, most people feel guilty even imagining it*. And the closest thing you have to not indulging is feeding voyeristically while someone else hunts.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Saying &quot;you have to hurt people to live is not new&quot; completely misses the entire point. Beast's take is vastly different than any other gameline, and not just because of metaphors. Its the very underlying reasoning and assumptions that make up the hurt that makes all the difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> * as per Psychology Today, which I think is a fairly reputable site. Feel free to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-22-2017, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T06:58:30-07:00","id":1066280,"title":"","content":"I would argue blood dolls are more similar to junkies than blood donors. Not to the same extent as ghouls to be sure but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:27:27-07:00","id":1066295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066274#post1066274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, its also no small part in that the hurting is differently from vampire, werewolf or changeling. Vampire blood dolls can be compared to a blood donor at Red Cross, and the feeding can take any form from mystical rite to sex to loyalty. And it feels good for all involved. Werewolves... well, eating humans is actually rare; most hunts against humans don't involve death and injury, and even when it does, the suffering is over quickly. Changelings snack on willpower, something that is so ephemeral you might not even realize it, through any kind of emotions. Sex, sports, and working in funeral homes are all valid and pretty harmless ways of feeding. Hells, I have Enchanting Performance on my current 'ling, and he can basically give out Inspired at will. Take glamour from lots of people, they all lose one point of willpower, but they get it back from Inspired, ending up in a net gain of glamour for the changeling and no loss for the humans. Demons have people willingly sign the dotted line, and neither mages nor prommies feed off people at all.<br /> <br /> Beasts feed on suffering and pain and loss. They're naturally sadistic, and the nature of that sadistic Hunger makes it hard to figure out ways to balance it out with some kind of positive event. You have to make people -hurt-. Not just physically, but on an emotional level, which, by many, is considered far worse than just a physical hurt you might not even feel. Beasts want to pull people off the hill and enjoy the thrill of their loss. In a very real way, its a game about indulging sadism, and that's not something many people are comfortable doing. Hells, most people feel guilty even imagining it*. And the closest thing you have to not indulging is feeding voyeristically while someone else hunts.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Saying &quot;you have to hurt people to live is not new&quot; completely misses the entire point. Beast's take is vastly different than any other gameline, and not just because of metaphors. Its the very underlying reasoning and assumptions that make up the hurt that makes all the difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> * as per Psychology Today, which I think is a fairly reputable site. Feel free to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast just takes the romanticized aspects away from hurting people, by not letting you cover up what you are <i>really </i>doing.<br /> <br /> Blood dolls being like blood donors? I don't recall blood donors being addicted to the experience and the person drawing the blood. The varied methods of drinking someone's blood does not change the fact that you're still drinking blood. Feels good for everyone... well, drugs certainly feel good.<br /> Yes, hunts don't have to target humans as the prey, nor do hunts end in killing the prey... But collateral damage is a thing. Humans simply <i>get in the way</i>. Lunacy from witnessing werewolves in action, organizations wrecked in the more abstract hunts, cultivating Resonance that affects people's minds and behaviors, or just plain ol' Death Rage ripping apart people unlucky enough to pass by.<br /> Don't remember word-for-word how the previewed Changeling rules work, but if changelings do drain Willpower... how can the victims not realize it? Willpower isn't just meta-narrative fuel for players to spend on behalf of their characters. It reflects how mentally and emotionally energetic a person is. Spend too much Willpower, and you feel down in the dumps, so you take a nap to rest or indulge in potentially unhealthy habitual behaviors (ie. Vices) Feeding on emotions is generally subtle, but changelings have an incentive to aggravate and exaggerate the emotions people feel... and with example emotions like Desire, Wrath, Fear, and Sorrow, I wouldn't want a changeling running around near me.<br /> Demons have people willingly sign the dotted line, yeah. So do loan sharks. And those elaborate contracts that technically tell you everything you need to know in the fine print.<br /> Mage's don't feed on people, but they can screw up Sleeper lives around them in a million ways. If the leaking Nimbuses, Quiescence, unsafely relinquished spells, and Paradoxes don't do it, then the mages treating Sleepers as pawns on the way to satisfy their Obsessions will.<br /> Prometheans... really? The guys who poison the world and peoples' minds by slipping up in some journey that they aren't clear on the details?<br /> <br /> Now of course, all the above supernaturals grant ways to mitigate the damage you do like you said. Which I find worse, because they're lying to themselves how they aren't monsters, when they're responsible or disciplined monsters at best. Beast, on the other hand, throws that veneer outside the window.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:49:23-07:00","id":1066303,"title":"","content":"So, to summarise, Beast does a lot of the same things as the other game lines. but is a bit more on-the-nose about it. Some consider that a good thing, others consider that a bad thing. <br /> <br /> Now, lets not derail the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:02:26-07:00","id":1066307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066303#post1066303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, lets not derail the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best words yet. Back to the Locker","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:02:26-07:00","id":1066308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066303#post1066303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, lets not derail the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best words yet. Back to the Locker","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:02:26-07:00","id":1066309,"title":"","content":"Triple post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:13:28-07:00","id":1066316,"title":"","content":"All very interesting. So when you play Beast, are you basically a human with the monster's powers, or do you have the ability to become the actual monster (i.e. shapeshifting), or are you not in human form at all?<br /> <br /> Does the Demon book allow you to play as Angels as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:19:57-07:00","id":1066320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066316#post1066316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All very interesting. So when you play Beast, are you basically a human with the monster's powers, or do you have the ability to become the actual monster (i.e. shapeshifting), or are you not in human form at all?<br /> <br /> Does the Demon book allow you to play as Angels as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your a monster in a human's body. You have powers but they aren't visible to most, you can take on the form of your &quot;true self&quot; but this is just about a last resort. You have some powers to reveal aspects of your true nature but generally there is no shape shifting. At least that's my understanding. With demon I'm not so certain but I'd assume being an angel would be like being an agent from the Matrix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:21:58-07:00","id":1066322,"title":"","content":"Demon is an Angel :P ex Angel.<br /> <br /> Beast issues as a game and a book are complicated and honestly are best served by reading the book on your own having little information on it beforehand, then soaking some context of history around it, and then reading other peoples opinion to compare them with your own. Opinions about the game are very polarized and &quot;why Beast is a god medicore terrible game&quot; discussions tend to end up very heated and flammable, so if you want to form your own opinion, I would really advise going in unbiased, so you can give the game justice.<br /> And I say that as a Beast hater who almost decided to stop following OPP's books after experiencing it due to massive distaste[I liked the basic concept, found execution unforgivable]. If you are interested in my opinion about it, or why I feel like that, feel free to PM me; I don't feel safe and comfortable enough discussing it here in public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:30:02-07:00","id":1066324,"title":"","content":"Yeah, probably not a good idea to do Lets Read: Beast. I can see that thread crashing and burning pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:32:32-07:00","id":1066326,"title":"","content":"Hurt Locker also gives you the option to be aggressively pacifistic. Plain Reader+ Empath+ Peacemaker. Throw in &quot;Damn Lucky&quot; and &quot;Ghost Pains&quot; and you can take people out without throwing a single punch. They fall over exhausted from punching your face in. It's so violent even the hardcore pacifists can mess you up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:33:53-07:00","id":1066327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066316#post1066316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All very interesting. So when you play Beast, are you basically a human with the monster's powers, or do you have the ability to become the actual monster (i.e. shapeshifting), or are you not in human form at all?<br /> <br /> Does the Demon book allow you to play as Angels as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Beast, the answer is generally no. There are a couple of exceptions, but usually the only way to take monstrous form is to either retreat into your Lair or impose your Lair on reality. <br /> <br /> For Demon, there are no rules for playing Angels. Angels with the amount of free will to be player characters by definition have fallen and become Demons, or have become cut off from the God Machine and become Exiles. Angels are really suited for narrative role because they lack free will and because they use the ephemeral entity rules (which are not used for player characters. Now with that said, if you really wanted to, you could come up with some rule hackssince there is a 2e Werewolf supplement that provide some very basic rules for using spirits as characters. Also, Geist 2e is supposedly going to feature rules for playing bonified ghosts as their &quot;minor&quot; splat (aka not the book's main focus, but a related &quot;lesser&quot; character type. Vampire's minor splat are Ghouls, and Werewolf's minor splat is the Wolf-Blooded, both of which are featured in their respective book's 1st appendix. Something similar to minor splats are also going to pop up in Hurt Locker, but I won't spoil the details for you). If we do get hard and fast rules for playing ghosts as PCs, they would most likely be useable to play angels as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:40:03-07:00","id":1066329,"title":"","content":"Oh, and for Mage, one of best comparisons to it was, at least for me, Doctor Who. Not because of the abilities of characters involved, but because these stories tend to capture what Mage &quot;is&quot; about - unstoppable, unsatable curiosity of someone very human emotionally, but also very inhuman when it comes to perspective and mentality. Just like Mages, The Doctor is a mystery junkie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:46:48-07:00","id":1066336,"title":"","content":"I did start reading the next chapter a little last night but didn't get through enough content to make a meaningful post. Will continue with that today after work. Did get through some of the new Merits but haven't delved into the Fighting stuff yet. So let's save that discussion for my next big post (hopefully coming tonight). Since I'm still at work and can't read the book at the moment, I'm curious to know if anyone read my play-by-post that I linked in the first thread and what your thoughts are? I may have put more effort into the layout than the actual game so far. I added a cover art now too. I didn't draw the cover art, but I have licensed it, so I've modified the colors of it and I can show it up to a maximum of 500,000 people before I need to pay more money. All of the photos I've added to the layout are from my Adobe Stock subscription too, and thus licensed as well. The only thing I'm not sure of is the Wikipedia/Linkedin stuff and the Chronicles of Darkness condition card. I could easily edit that away but I prefer not to since I think it looks good. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:50:53-07:00","id":1066337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066329#post1066329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and for Mage, one of best comparisons to it was, at least for me, Doctor Who. Not because of the abilities of characters involved, but because these stories tend to capture what Mage &amp;quot;is&amp;quot; about - unstoppable, unsatable curiosity of someone very human emotionally, but also very inhuman when it comes to perspective and mentality. Just like Mages, The Doctor is a mystery junkie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god yes. And the whole theme of discovering and exploring strange worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:51:55-07:00","id":1066339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066329#post1066329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and for Mage, one of best comparisons to it was, at least for me, Doctor Who. Not because of the abilities of characters involved, but because these stories tend to capture what Mage &quot;is&quot; about - unstoppable, unsatable curiosity of someone very human emotionally, but also very inhuman when it comes to perspective and mentality. Just like Mages, The Doctor is a mystery junkie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that Atlantis/The Time Before is basically New Series!Gallifrey. It no longer exists anywhere in the Timeline, but weird shit from &quot;The Time War&quot; keep popping up everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:02:35-07:00","id":1066347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066336#post1066336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did start reading the next chapter a little last night but didn't get through enough content to make a meaningful post. Will continue with that today after work. Did get through some of the new Merits but haven't delved into the Fighting stuff yet. So let's save that discussion for my next big post (hopefully coming tonight). Since I'm still at work and can't read the book at the moment, I'm curious to know if anyone read my play-by-post that I linked in the first thread and what your thoughts are? I may have put more effort into the layout than the actual game so far. I added a cover art now too. I didn't draw the cover art, but I have licensed it, so I've modified the colors of it and I can show it up to a maximum of 500,000 people before I need to pay more money. All of the photos I've added to the layout are from my Adobe Stock subscription too, and thus licensed as well. The only thing I'm not sure of is the Wikipedia/Linkedin stuff and the Chronicles of Darkness condition card. I could easily edit that away but I prefer not to since I think it looks good. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's little hard for me to navigate, because my device hates PDFs. It's pretty, but little unwieldly and navigating it annoys me, because I can't easily find the place where I dropped off last time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:46:51-07:00","id":1066392,"title":"","content":"I adored your playthrough pdf. I've always collated my playthrough documents, and my girlfriend has recently started recording chapters again, but I've never put up something like that online. I may suggest something similar be distributed at the end of stories in my local game, now :P<br /> Excellent cover, by the way. I like the article, the character sheet, and the framing thus far has been both clear and entertaining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:22:42-07:00","id":1066430,"title":"","content":"I noticed nobody has tried to summarize Mummy, so I'll take up the mantle and scribe something out...<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy: The Curse</b> was the last 1st Edition Chronicles line before the new edition, but also represents the most thorough usage of the 1E-isms and conceits, such as weaving the 7 Virtues/Vices into the mechanics and powers and doing a <i>lot</i> with ghosts. By the same token, it's one of the strangest. In every CofD line before it, characters started off as fresh-faced newbs at the nadir of their power. They went from being naive greenhorns to (maybe) being uncontested supernatural badasses, full of power and knowledge.<br /> <br /> Mummy deliberately inverts that advancement scheme. Mummies are all ancient beings, gathered together in a Stone Age African Empire and ritually sacrificed by Sorcerer Kings, bound to wander between the afterlife and this waking world doing the bidding of Dark Cosmic Gods called the Judges. Mummies are awakened by cults dedicated to them to carry out tasks, usually in the name of the Judges. When Mummies awaken they are at the zenith of their power: surging with divine power so intense their bodies can't even properly form around them (leaving them looking like walking desiccated corpses). As time passes, the power starts to dwindle, and a proper human shell grows around them so they can start to properly interact with human civilization. Eventually the power dwindles to almost nothing and they return to a state of death-like hibernation as their spirits descend once again into the underworld.<br /> <br /> However, their memories are by design left shattered and torn. They awaken at the height of their power, but with almost no knowledge beyond their Purpose, their name, and scattered recollections of their previous awakening. As time passes and their power drains, they trigger flashbacks that let them regain their memories and start to piece together their many, many pasts and, most importantly, their identity. As a game, it's possible to run through multiple awakenings (called Descents) and have different players play the same mummy each time since the resetting of Memory means that they might behave like a different person (albeit with the same Virtue/Vice).<br /> <br /> It's fascinating but naturally the weird nature of the game puts some people off. For me it was what got me back into the entire Chronicles of Darkness after a 5-year hiatus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:34:52-07:00","id":1066441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066430#post1066430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a game, it's possible to run through multiple awakenings (called Descents) and have different players play the same mummy each time since the resetting of Memory means that they might behave like a different person (albeit with the same Virtue/Vice).</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah, cool! I'd never thought about that, but that's an awesome idea. I do want to try Mummy at some point, but I think I would have to play it first before I'll be able to grasp it well enough to run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:43:59-07:00","id":1066448,"title":"","content":"Also saw that no one has done Changeling yet. I'm willing to do it, since I'm obsessed with it, but do you think we should wait until the 2nd Edition Changeling book comes out to see the full extent of the changes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:44:39-07:00","id":1066449,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, I like the themes of mummy, and I'd definitely play it at some point (Though I'd almost definitely play a cultist and not the Mummy itself) but if I ever wanted to run the themes of mummy I'd probably use Mekhet ancients instead....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:44:50-07:00","id":1066450,"title":"","content":"Looking at the splats from another point of view<br /> <br /> Vampire: you're a pale glorified mosquito who has to distract itself from how horrible its unlife is by playing a massive game of pointless politics and needlessly complicated intrigue because if you don't then you realize how terrible everything is, possibly attract an evil owl thing, go batty(heh) and end up becoming a ravenous monster.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: you're some poor schmuck with really bad anger issues and the ability to turn into a number of wolf themed animal forms. Also you're an animist and have to deal with a game of pointless politics and needlessly complicated intrigue with the spirit world because if you don't you'll realize just how terrible everything is, an angry spirit will probably murder your family and you end up becoming a ravenous monster.<br /> <br /> Mage: you are Ebony Dark'ness Dementia Raven Way, a seventh year slytherin who's overwhelmingly beautiful and has Draco Malfoy wrapped around your finger. You spend your time dealing with pointless wizard politics and needlessly complicated intrigue, hiding your magic away from the Muggles because if you don't then you'll probably attract the attention of an unspeakable Cthulhu horror who will eat your family or you make a deal with it and become a ravenous monster. Or it would be that way but you took three dots in time magic.<br /> <br /> Promethean: you're Frankenstein's monster with extra magical powers, your whole life sucks and you ruin everyone and everything around you just by existing. You're on your journey to learn how to become a real boy but have to constantly move around or risk attracting the attention of malformed abominations that eat your soul energy or despoiling the land around you into an apocalyptic wasteland, occasionally the pressure of it all gets to you and you might end up becoming a ravenous monster.<br /> <br /> Changeling: you were kidnapped by faeries and taken to their magical land where they stripped you of any semblance of humanity and tortured you for an indeterminate amount of time, possibly decades, until you escaped. Now your soul is all torn to bits, you have magical powers, a tenuous grasp on sanity and are being hunted by those faeries who very much would like you back. So you spend your time dealing with pointless politics and needlessly complicated intrigue trying to remain hidden because if you don't then you'll realize how terrible everything is, go crazy and end up becoming just as bad the the things that kidnapped you, or you'll just get kidnapped and subjugated again.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters: i actually don't know much about this, you're a dude who died and got a powerful \u00fcber-ghost sharing space with your soul, now you're a ghost buster with magical powers who spends your time at pointless raves and needlessly complicated orgies until the \u00fcber-ghost gets on your ass about completing some unknown goal. You're also really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really, really hard to kill.<br /> <br /> Mummy: again, don't know much. You're a dude who died a long time ago but due to an ancient ritual you keep coming back. You are filled with a burning obsession for something, though you may not know what and nothing will stop you from completing that goal even if it takes centuries, or even if you don't know what that goal is. You start out powerful but grow weaker as you spend time out and about, having only a small amount of time to complete that goal before returning back to your deathlike slumber only to return when you are called upon again or after some kind of thousand year cycle. And you're probably impossible to kill, that's about what I got.<br /> <br /> Beast: not quite sure on this one, you're a person who either had their soul eaten by a nightmare creature or you were that nightmare creature all along. Now you are basically Freddy Kreuger if he had better PR but probably without the urge to brutally murder everyone you meet... Probably. You have to go out and eat people's dreams because if you don't then the ravenous monster inside of you does it for you and is a lot less gentle about it, which then either creates or attracts an army of Gastons from beauty in the beast to come kill you. Also you are like everyone's third cousin or something like that, my knowledge of beast(as with sin-eaters and mummy) is very spotty.<br /> <br /> Demons: not the Judeo-Christian variety, you're just called a demon for convenience sake. You're actually some kind of weird biomechanical abomination that used to work for a nigh-omnipotent computer God but now you've escaped and are hiding from the computer god's &quot;angels&quot;. To do that though you need to blend in, so you get into contracts and bargains with mortals in the hopes of taking over their life and exploring your new found free will.<br /> <br /> Hunter: you're a normal dude(sometimes) with a little more information on what's really going on in the world(sometimes) and you're angry about it(sometimes). However you are hopelessly outmatched against everything else in the world(most of the time) so you have to vent your frustrations out on bargain bin monsters that still are probably more than a match for you(sometimes).<br /> <br /> This is the uneducated man's opinion at a glance, and how I describe it to friends who ask me about the games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:52:05-07:00","id":1066454,"title":"","content":"The Changeling one actually started out like a pretty accurate summary of the game up until the running &quot;needless politics&quot; gag. I got a few chuckles out of the whole thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:54:12-07:00","id":1066457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066450#post1066450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You spend your time dealing with pointless [x] politics and needlessly complicated intrigue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard the entirety of Chronicles of Darkness summed up so well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:55:43-07:00","id":1066458,"title":"","content":"That werewolf one is more than a bit off. They don't particularly have anger issues, for instance, and one isn't obligated to involve themselves in spirit politics, though it helps. Also you'd worry more about another werewolf or host murdering your family, as that's not really a spirit thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:58:28-07:00","id":1066460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066458#post1066458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't particularly have anger issues</div> </div> </div> </div>...are, are you sure about that? Considering they have a mechanic literally called &quot;Death Rage&quot; I'm not sure that can be said with total honesty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:01:53-07:00","id":1066465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066460#post1066460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...are, are you sure about that? Considering they have a mechanic literally called &quot;Death Rage&quot; I'm not sure that can be said with total honesty.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have ubiquitous anger issues though. They have 4-7 very specific triggers that set off their spiritual instincts. It's different from Apocalypse and 1E Forsaken where anger was sort of a constant that 'wolves had to worry about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:02:24-07:00","id":1066466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066460#post1066460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...are, are you sure about that? Considering they have a mechanic literally called &quot;Death Rage&quot; I'm not sure that can be said with total honesty.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a supernatural effect. Saying they have anger issues is saying mages spontaneously summon things because abyssal entities might appear during paradox, or Prometheans have poor people skills because of Disquiet. A werewolf can be a serene and tranquil agent of peace if you wanted to play that way.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/World_of_Darkness#New_World_of_Darkness.2FChronicles_of_Darkness_.28nWoD.2FCoD.29\" target=\"_blank\">1d4chan's</a> summaries were better. I don't get the point of harping on needless politics, in every game it's as important or nonimportant as you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:04:40-07:00","id":1066467,"title":"","content":"2E werewolves arguably have a better lid on their rage than vampires do. Kuruth can only be triggered by a few moderately specific things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:04:42-07:00","id":1066468,"title":"","content":"They're all pretty accurate summaries, especially if you want to run a blended game. The personalized 'intrigue' tends to be a bit melodramatic at best, especially given its emphasis on <i>Thematic Angst</i>, and at worst actively works against cohesive storytelling and narrative. They work, as they are, ideally in a vacuum with no impetus for real change; this despite that every template has a sect devoted exclusively to change.<br /> The thing is, you're not expected to run them straight out of the book, and that conceit is something that should probably be better advertised :P<br /> <br /> And just an addendum, I've never had a Sin-Eater attend a party that wasn't some kind of memorial holiday, and I made sure people were culturally appropriate for the same. People tend to be more excited about the powers and death-tainted world they can explore than the loose mishmash 'culture' presented in the book; some of the fiction supports that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:06:10-07:00","id":1066470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066454#post1066454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Changeling one actually started out like a pretty accurate summary of the game up until the running &amp;quot;needless politics&amp;quot; gag. I got a few chuckles out of the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it felt kind of forced for me too. They have freehold politics I think but I don't think it's necessarily pointless since the whole idea is a safety net so you don't go insane and you have something to fall back on when the faeries come to get you. It's actually kind of hard to make changeling sound darker than it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:10:06-07:00","id":1066474,"title":"","content":"I thought the summaries were pretty good for what they were - humorous summaries viewed from &quot;the outside.&quot; Nobody's saying you <i>have </i>to focus on pointless politics in any of the games, only that the games do usually encourage it via the various factions.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> I completely agree with you. Vampires <i>also </i>have serious anger issues. This should definitely be taken into account.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:15:56-07:00","id":1066477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066467#post1066467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2E werewolves arguably have a better lid on their rage than vampires do. Kuruth can only be triggered by a few moderately specific things.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, I'm just kind of stuck in a 1E mindset for a lot of the games. I keep forgetting about Vampire Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:56:30-07:00","id":1066535,"title":"","content":"Demons are actually rather Judeo-Christian (as mush as I dislike that term) really, they just aren't Renaissance Artist Roman Catholic Demons. They fit the descriptions in the Bible much more than the paintings of 17th Century Italy ever did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T13:20:23-07:00","id":1066543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066535#post1066535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons are actually rather Judeo-Christian (as mush as I dislike that term) really, they just aren't Renaissance Artist Roman Catholic Demons. They fit the descriptions in the Bible much more than the paintings of 17th Century Italy ever did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps but they don't fit the mold in so far as origins go. They might resemble Gnostic demons on that front. I actually rather liked the machine aspect and use a sort of hybrid of inferno and descent demons for my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T13:26:32-07:00","id":1066544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066543#post1066543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps but they don't fit the mold in so far as origins go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they do. Angels that disobey orders and Fall from Grace? That's classic Demon material right there.<br /> <br /> Really, the machine stuff is 90% superficial aesthetic detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T13:29:54-07:00","id":1066547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066544#post1066544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure they do. Angels that disobey orders and Fall from Grace? That's classic Demon material right there.<br /> <br /> Really, the machine stuff is 90% superficial aesthetic detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring more to the God-Machine. The whole demiurge thing is really a Gnostic tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T13:34:28-07:00","id":1066549,"title":"","content":"Time to reign in the discussion now. I appreciate all the info on the different splats and I do have follow-up questions, but I'll hold on to those for now since the thread isn't really about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T14:44:57-07:00","id":1066582,"title":"","content":"This (speaking on your last chapter read) is something that I always strive for but am usually not satisfied with my attempts. Show-not-telling as far as violence goes.<br /> <br /> One of the things that I do focus on in my games is portraying <i>action scenes</i> rather than <i>fight scenes </i>for basically anything that would require initiative rolls. I treat them more how a movie or a show would treat scenes when the tempo of the music swells to erratic levels. This I'm proud of. What I struggle with, I think, is portraying each turn as more narrativly important than &quot;doing this much damage in this area&quot; or &quot;you pull ahead in the foot chase&quot;. Sometimes these scenes feel organic but other times I think I fall back on the descriptions.<br /> <br /> Anyway that was just something I thought about while you read the chapter.<br /> <br /> <b>(||</b>EDIT: sorry, I started writing this before you reigned in the topic and it took me a while to write ^.^; The above part is topic appropriate though ^.^;<b>||)</b><br /> <br /> And here's my brief descriptions of the splats, I've read most of the splats and played about half of them so here's my attempt at clarifying them for you. I think other's have done a better job than I can with explaining the splats to you but i'm going to try for laconic explanations.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>: Humans that are turned (or sired) into one of the Kindred with traits depending on the clan (or typical vampire tropes) of their Sire.<br /> <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b>: Half human/Half Wolf-Spirit Uratha (forsaken in spirit-tongue) who are tasked by the spirit of the moon with keeping the borders between the Shadow (spirit) and physical realms balanced.<br /> <b>Mage: The Awakened</b>: A human whose soul becomes connected to a Supernal Realm of magic allowing them to work their will on physical realm depending on their studies and knowledge.<br /> <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b>: A loose collection of humans who've seen what goes bump in the night and so have become inspired to hunt (a vigil is sparked) and fight various things for various reasons.<br /> <b>Promethean: The Created</b>: An artificial being* brought to life by the Divine Fire (a fake soul) who pilgrimages to refine their Divine Fire into a human soul.<br /> <b>Changeling: The Lost</b>: Human stolen to Arcadia (the Faerie realm) by a True Fae and tormented and broken (physically, emotionally, and mentally) till they do whatever job (**) given to them. Some find their way back only to find their life was replaced by a <i>thing</i>, they are still irreparably changed by their durance, and they are actively hunted by their captors.<br /> <b>Geist: The Sin-Eaters</b>: Humans who agree to fuse with Geists (very powerful Ghosts essentially) in return for coming back to life who now can see ghosts and share their Geist's ghost-like powers.<br /> <b>Mummy: The Curse</b>: An ancient immortal that does the bidding of a Judge (a type of death-god) and protects an artifact but can only be awake for a period of time before resting for centuries.<br /> <b>Demon: The Descent</b>: Angels of the God-Machine who become <i>unhooked</i> and <i>Fall (becoming physical)</i> after questioning or disobeying (***) one of their functions and now is hunted to be <i>Recycled</i> (regardless of the circumstances of the <i>Fall</i>).<br /> <b>Beast: The Primordial</b>: A (seemingly) human whose soul is that of a Primordial Fear Horror causing them to feed on mortals in a plethora of ways but must fight and survive <i>Heroes </i>(People who have the compulsion to hunt a specific Beast).<br /> <b>Deviant: The Renegades</b>: (take this with a grain of salt as it's not out yet) A human who had something done to them by someone (scientists, monsters, yourself, &amp;c) giving you abilities that, are at best, unstable and are now hunted by various organizations and individuals.<br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> *<b>Note on Promethean</b>: The being can be created out of anything but used flesh is pretty common. The important thing is they are artificial (Frankenstein's Monster, the Golem, the boy from A.I., &amp;c)<br /> <br /> **<b>Note on Changeling</b>: They are changed depending on their master's intended function for them which can be anything from caterer, sex-slave, gardener, doll, &amp;c to things like a plant, statue, candle fire, hunter's hounds, the sun, the walls of a cliff, one of many glow-worms in a cave, and other weirder things. Additional note: Changelings become at least humanoid when entering the Physical realm.<br /> <br /> ***<b>Note on Demon</b>: Sometimes the <i>Fall</i> happens on accident and sometimes the Angel's function seems to be counter, say, another angels function. So the now Demon may not have ever wanted to fall. Regardless, they are now vigorously hunted with the end result being dismantled for spare parts.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 03-22-2017, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T15:45:26-07:00","id":1066606,"title":"","content":"Okay, I haven't caught up to Ekorren yet, but I have shit to say about the first part of the chapter, so I'm going to get it out.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Chapter 1: Stories of Violence</u><br /> <br /> Storytelling Violence (aka Oh God the Feels)</b><br /> <br /> David is awesome. David's team is awesome. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a>, if you are reading this, you are awesome. This entire section is stuff that is so hard to right, so easy to phone in, but it wasn't. Hell, I'd go as far to say that this should be outright required reading for all GMs in all game systems. Wes Schneider wrote a similar section in Pathfinder's Horror Adventures about the dos and don'ts of running a horror game. They are different topics, but they compliment each other fantastically.<br /> <br /> (In fact, I can think of one Dracula-esque nuWWP personality who could really learn something from both books, but I digress...)<br /> <br /> I'm going to go a bit out of order here, but that is to compose my thoughts in a rational manner. The Stories About Lasting Harm and Stories About Moving on sections really reasonate with me. I am somewhat luck in that the only major violence event in my life was at the hands of nature rather than the hands of a person and I have been sheltered from most possible forms of violence. That said, I still got nailed hard by PTSD. I also moved on from it after a solid 11 years. This section is so senstive to the uniqueness and individuality of trauma and it warms my heart. I think that using Vices to represent difficulty moving on is a really cool idea and I LOVE using the idea of specialities to represent moving on with your life. If I were stating myself up in real life, I could see giving myself Survival (avalanches) or Medicine (CPR) for exactly that reason. I threw myself into both and have kept them up to date for most of my adult life.<br /> <br /> Moving backwards to the Eschewing Labels sidebar and the Stories About Victims/Victimizers sections. The whole concept of avoiding both labels and moral judgement here is so important. Here's my real-life justification. I teach at a school that specializes in students with learning disabilities, although I prefer to think of it as aneurotypicallity. But then again, I would think that because I have had effective strategies to deal with my own LD since Middle School. It is similar to ADHD at a glance but is actually an entirely different neurology, which means that drugs do nothing because it is the result of my long term memory being in the 95th percentile and while my short term memory is in the 9th percentile based on the WISC-III and later the WIAT-II.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, one of the things that we observe in our student populations (and those of us staff who have LDs ourselves) is that there is a very high incidence of low-esteem, low-self-worth, and low-affect when they come to our school. You could make a strong argument that this is all trauma and violence based. It is important to note, though, that I'm not talking about violence. I'm talking about the experience of trying to make the square peg fit in the round hole. The experience of not being able to relate to your peers. The experience of socially, emotionally, and/or academically behind your peers because your brain is developing at different rates and in different ways than &quot;normal.&quot; Accidental (as well as intentional) mental violence happens to these populations. Does that mean that other schools who don't know how or can't appropriately accommodate these individuals are victimizers? Probably not. Are the students themselves victims? I suspect that most of them would say no. It depends on context. A well-meaning person that is out of their depth or not properly supported can do tons of harm without even realizing it. Any mature treatment of violence has to acknowledge that nuance.<br /> <br /> I liked the summaries of the different gamelines, but I'm a bit disappointed that there was nothing mentioned past Hunter. Geist, Mummy, Demon, and Beast all could have benefited from that discussion.<br /> <br /> I will fully admit to completely skipping Integrity by Attrition on my first skim. I think that was the point when turned straight to the micro-template merits. It is a pretty cool system, though, and both of the merits are solid. I may use a variant of it in my next Vampire game. The optional system won't work with all game lines, but Vampire, Mage, Hunter, and possibly Changeling should be able to utilize it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-22-2017, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T19:41:47-07:00","id":1066677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066448#post1066448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also saw that no one has done Changeling yet. I'm willing to do it, since I'm obsessed with it, but do you think we should wait until the 2nd Edition Changeling book comes out to see the full extent of the changes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looking at the draft, ain't that different. We just have Middle Managers of Evil/Emotional Abuse now.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling: the Lost</b><br /> <br /> First of all: Congratulations! You escaped the most seductive and addicting form of slavery in the cosmos! Too bad the humanity your former owner removed to fit a collar didn't come back with you. <br /> <br /> Yeah, all those stories about faerie lords and ladies abducting human children and replacing them with their own species? Yeah, two errors; one, it's not so much a fae so much as it is a golem formed from a piece of their new possession's soul, and two, they abduct <i>everyone. </i>What the rationale was varies and, let's be frank, does not matter; it all comes down to the fact that a True Fae, the lunatic aristocracy-gods of Arcadia, decided he or she (it, zhe, he and she...) needed you for something, or because you broke a meaningless law, or both (probably more likely both than the second option). You were stolen and replaced by a fetch, a clone of you with <i>something </i>missing (although in well-made fetches that thing tends to be trivial or something you would be glad to be rid of), and taken on a rough ride through Hedge, the border-world that lies between Earth and Arcadia, losing most of your soul on its Thorns in the process. Now properly malleable, your Keeper reshaped you into an ideal servant-but because the True Fae are psychotically self-centered (to the point where they fear the Hedge even more than changelings; the Thorns are composed of the pain of all sentient life, and thus a Keeper cut by them starts to <i>emphasize</i>), you were never good enough-and yet, your Keeper still <i>valued </i>you, because of how versatile you were as a servant. Your life, what little your now-mostly-human intellect recalls, was a wild swing between joy and misery, usually the latter. At some point though, there was a break; perhaps the shifting politics of Faerie suddenly manifested you in a physical form, perhaps even as a song you had enough of a mind to recognize how you were treated; in any case, you realized how addictive Arcadia is really does not balance the horror of eternal servitude, and so you tore out the part of you convinced that, somehow, this was worth it (literally, it's a magic artifact called an icon), and fled into-and out of-the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the True Fae love their servants, in their sick, myopic way. They <i>notice </i>when you're gone-and even beyond that, Lost like you are prize catches by other Keepers due to the allure of your mustang soul.If that wasn't enough, you're no longer sane in any human way; how can you be, when your very body is composed of living metaphor for how you escaped and your intended duty? (On a good day, you're not actually insane, either-about half of your hallucinations are prophetic visions, the problem is telling the difference.) You desperately need someone who understands-but thankfully, you aren't alone. You may be a rare breed, but only in proportion, and it's always a goal of some brave and/or stupid changelings to give their Kept brethren opportunity to escape. So you find a <i>freehold </i>of fellow escapees and rebels, and use your newfound relationship with Fate (the Wyrd that all fae, you included, loves it some tales) and made yourselves characters in a legend about how you keep the True Fae away-and they have no choice but to obey, because they've never been anything but story (as far as they know or care).<br /> <br /> But be warned-besides a fetch who feels it's <i>their </i>life, thank you very much (you may or may not agree), legends demand conflict-and that means politics between a race of people composed entirely of those too stubborn to give up, And the True Fae are crafty; <i>they </i>can't insert themselves in the legend, but <i>their servants </i>can...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T20:53:22-07:00","id":1066691,"title":"","content":"Catching, catching, caught up. Time for my part 2 of Chapter 1: Why didn't I read these parts the first time? <br /> <br /> <b>Framing Scenes </b><br /> I definitely did not process these correctly the first time I read them. They make much more sense now. Framing scenes are an easy, punchy system to use that can give some much-needed pizzazz to a scene. The examples are all good, and some them are straight up &quot;build around me&quot; ideas like speeding train, free fall, and high steel. <br /> <br /> <b>Violence Groups</b><br /> Another section I mostly skipped on my first pass. Absolutely fantastic. Treating the group similar to an NPC with simplified stats is a sublime way to make them an actual threat. A bunch of gangbangers don't stand a chance against a Mummy in a head to head conflict, but as a collective, they can still cause problems. Giving the groups aspirations, &quot;virtues&quot;, and vices is also a good way to give the mooks some personality and some insight into how the group functions. I bet you could translate Violence Groups into specific gamelines pretty effectively. Even if I flesh out every member of a werewolf pack, defining the pack's aspirations, virtue, and vice is a good practice for the storyteller. It's also a nice way to have cults crop up that aren't overtly supernatural like the Mystery Cult Initiation implies. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:45:44-07:00","id":1066823,"title":"","content":"I don't think it was pointed out before, but Integrity by Attrition gives you a way to recover Integrity without paying Experience. This solves a common problem and critique about Integrity and Integrity equivalents: they can and will be lost through roleplaying, but cost you the same resource (XP) that is spent on permanent things, which turns losing Integrity into &quot;too bad, you are now going to be 2 XP behind everyone else because they don't have to be punished for failing an Integrity check&quot;.<br /> This applies to most of the Integrity replacements in the game lines, too. &quot;Recover Humanity through roleplaying event for no XP cost&quot; is a common homerule. It's also pretty obnoxious in Mage, where you need to spend a whole story trying to up your Wisdom just so you can spend XP to bring it up by one, and you lose control of your character at Wisdom 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-23-2017, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:47:32-07:00","id":1066825,"title":"","content":"Which is why my group awards 2 XP when losing Integrity/Humanity/Wisdom. We'd probably skip that for Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:58:32-07:00","id":1066833,"title":"","content":"I don't really like the idea that you'll have to buy back your Integrity. I prefer to let characters regain Integrity when it makes sense in the story. Maybe they go to therapy, try to seriously learn meditation, or tries to move past the trauma in ways that make sense in game. Is there anything in the rules that suggests that it is a bad idea to simply give back Integrity as the occasional story handout when I feel it makes sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:03:43-07:00","id":1066839,"title":"","content":"Nah, you can do it that way without breaking anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:32:45-07:00","id":1066860,"title":"","content":"Integrity by Attrition is pretty much that, with added gameplay element that allows you to track it easier and have a sense of progress towards your goal. Looking at legacy of games (both video, board and tabletop), getting to mark a halfway point between regaining a point and not regaining a point tends to make the halfway point almost as satisfying as reaching the end, while increasing feeling of player agency (&quot;I did a thing, and it made the bar towards my goal progress, I have a visual representation of my actions having consequences, so cool&quot;)<br /> This is BTW &quot;science&quot; behind tons of facebook clickey games and addiction to achievments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:50:01-07:00","id":1066873,"title":"","content":"I've been known to just ignore integrity rules at times, sometimes all the players going crazy in the middle of the chronicle messes up with the story. That and I'm incredibly lazy so I forget to do breaking point rolls a lot. My custom Sci-Fi game that uses the Storyteller System has the integrity rules just outright removed, but it's not supposed to be a horror game so it's different. When I can be bothered to remember to use integrity rules I usually have rules and safety nets in place to help stave off spiraling down the cliffs of insanity. The whole support network thing in Hurt Locker was a long time houserule, albeit with different incarnations. I use Hunter Tells in a similar function to Vampire Banes from VtR, which might not be a houserule but I haven't checked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:08:55-07:00","id":1066886,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Integrity suffers from the death spiral phenomena. The less you have, easier it is to lose it. So if you don't re-buy it fast, you are increasing your chance of losing more and more of it, costing you more experience. It also highlights one of Attribute system problems, where Composure and Resolve tend to do be worth more than other Attributes, simply because they contribute to a lot of subsystems. Specifically with Integrity in mind, they determine your pool for Breaking Points, which makes certain characters less likely to lose Integrity, so you can't expect all characters to fail around the same number of Breaking Points - contrast it with Wisdom in Mage, where each character has ~the same chance of passing Wisdom Checks, and math seems to be balanced that on a average, you will make enough Beats from Wisdom Breaking Points to restore it, and then have a net gain of one or two over course of the Chronicle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:22:29-07:00","id":1066894,"title":"","content":"1st Edition had a rule where a &quot;particularly redeeming, generous, or self-effacing act&quot; regained a free point of 'Morality X', and it's been nice to keep around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:46:33-07:00","id":1066904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrophear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066894#post1066894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st Edition had a rule where a &quot;particularly redeeming, generous, or self-effacing act&quot; regained a free point of 'Morality X', and it's been nice to keep around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But isn't Integrity more about how well you're keeping it together than moral standing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:09:02-07:00","id":1066925,"title":"","content":"As a translation to 2nd edition jargon (bear with me here, my lingo is off at best because I'm usually translating things the <i>other </i>direction):<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;When an Aspiration is attained, if appropriate your Storyteller may ask you to roll your Integrity/Humanity score in dice. Three or more successes will allow you to regain 1 Integrity/humanity for free, while seven successes will allow you to regain 2. </div> </div> </div>That allows the roll to be as subjective and common/uncommon as the ST deems it necessary, while tying it in with the character's personal goals; in this case representing achievement that reaffirms a character's esteem and confidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","user":"Necrophear","date":". 03-23-2017, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:32:09-07:00","id":1066947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066606#post1066606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">David is awesome. David's team is awesome. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a>, if you are reading this, you are awesome. This entire section is stuff that is so hard to right, so easy to phone in, but it wasn't. Hell, I'd go as far to say that this should be outright required reading for all GMs in all game systems. Wes Schneider wrote a similar section in Pathfinder's Horror Adventures about the dos and don'ts of running a horror game. They are different topics, but they compliment each other fantastically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh! Now I <i>really</i> can't wait till my copy comes in!!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Violence Groups</b><br /> Another section I mostly skipped on my first pass. Absolutely fantastic. Treating the group similar to an NPC with simplified stats is a sublime way to make them an actual threat. </div> </div> </div>I suppose I'll have to wait for my copy to come in for a real answer but is this section detailing an option for writing a group of npcs to have the same <i>turn</i> order of a single npc? If so, that would make the, usually laborious, task of having a large amount of NPC's in an action scene a lot easier to handle. (I and players get bored if I'm rolling 5 npcs in between a player. and for good reason)<br /> <br /> If this is true, I will likely def use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:12:15-07:00","id":1066974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1066886#post1066886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Integrity suffers from the death spiral phenomena. The less you have, easier it is to lose it. So if you don't re-buy it fast, you are increasing your chance of losing more and more of it, costing you more experience. It also highlights one of Attribute system problems, where Composure and Resolve tend to do be worth more than other Attributes, simply because they contribute to a lot of subsystems. Specifically with Integrity in mind, they determine your pool for Breaking Points, which makes certain characters less likely to lose Integrity, so you can't expect all characters to fail around the same number of Breaking Points - contrast it with Wisdom in Mage, where each character has ~the same chance of passing Wisdom Checks, and math seems to be balanced that on a average, you will make enough Beats from Wisdom Breaking Points to restore it, and then have a net gain of one or two over course of the Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, and how you like your integrity comes down to the preferences of one troupe to the next. <br /> <br /> I personally like the death spiral of integrity in my games because of a few reasons:<br /> - I am sometimes pretty generous with Experiences and beats.<br /> - My games are long but often don't last a very very long time. Meaning I've yet to see anyone actually reach the int 0 (I've seen Cover 0 I have but that's totally different).<br /> - I'm also pretty forgiving on when to roll for breaking points.<br /> - And lastly, the easy slip in integrity is a big background part in almost every one of my games. <br /> <br /> The above means that my players tend to one of the following:<br /> 1. They try hard to not lose integrity in the first place and so they wont more often than not.<br /> 2. They try and fail to not lose integrity and don't bother with regaining that dot due to rationalizing the breaking point away and thus compromise their values if even slightly.<br /> 3. They try and fail to not lose integrity but roleplay the breaking point and the loss of integrity and the desire for redemption or otherwise cannot rationalize it away which I would likely award special integrity beats for the roleplaying.<br /> <br /> I like it as a tool for the storytelling the spiral in my games. Half of my players are of the second kind and the other half are the third kind and both work <i>deliciously </i>as additions to the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T06:40:08-07:00","id":1068275,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>CHAPTER TWO: INSTRUMENTS OF VIOLENCE</b></span><br /> <br /> The chapter starts out with a list of general Merits that are designed for mortal characters but can be used for most splats, save from a few referencing mechanics that don't make sense for said splats. I'm going to go over the Merits from the book without revealing too much mechanical detail.<br /> <br /> <b>Air of Menace: </b>Enhances the character's ability to intimidate others but also makes sure to address the fact that looking menacing isn't always a good thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Body as Weapon: </b>Unarmed attacks deal more damage. It's interesting that it's Stamina-based instead of Strength-based, but I assume it has to do with hardened knuckles.<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesive Unit: </b>This is a powerful Merit for the social leader type character. It gives plenty of benefits to a team under the character's command.<br /> <br /> <b>Defender: </b>This Merit gives additional Willpower points specifically meant to be used to protect loved ones. I can't really address the balance of this one since my lack of experience with the game makes it so that only a single point of Willpower has been spent in my pbp so far, and that one was replenished quickly. This is a good Merit to have for the kind of games where you burn through Willpower quickly which I suppose a violence-heavy game does.<br /> <br /> <b>Empath: </b>The way this Merit explains how you can identify other character's Conditions is something I'd think you'd be able to do with an ordinary Empathy roll. It's not really difficult to see that someone is <i>Shaken </i>for example.<br /> <br /> <b>Object Fetishism: </b>Right. This Merit lets you create Negan from the Walking Dead. You associate a Skill Specialty with your favorite object and draws a bunch of additional Willpower and so forth. It's a very very powerful Merit for the character who has a favored weapon, like Negan's Lucile.<br /> <br /> <b>Peacemaker: </b>This is a very powerful Merit and a must-have for the kind of empathic, social character that wants to play pacifist.<br /> <br /> <b>Punch Drunk: </b>This Merit lets you keep fighting even after you should be knocked out. Very cool.<br /> <br /> <b>Scarred: </b>This is an interesting one. It lets you take on a persistent Condition when failing a breaking point. The only way to get rid of the Condition is to also get rid of this Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Support Network: </b>This Merit lets you prolong an Integrity breaking point for some time.<br /> <br /> <b>Survivalist: </b>You are more resistant to extreme cold or heat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FIGHTING MERITS</b><br /> <br /> The book changes the way Fighting Merits work from the rulebook by freeing them up and making them less structured. I like the change for the most part, but I think some styles have too strict requirements based on the limited number of dots you get at character creation.<br /> <br /> I enjoyed the paragraph about the arguments over the best style. When I was in grade school, I was a judo kid. I thought I was really cool at the time. As I became a teenager, I had watched a bunch of kung fu movies and started training hung gar kuen, tai chi and sanshou. I learned how to flail around while thinking I was cool. Then when I got older (17-18), I realized that I was bowing to altars in a dojo and talking about chi like some weird religious sect. I suddenly found the whole thing completely ridiculous and stopped doing it. But then again, I didn't train &quot;fighting&quot;. I went to a class where people imagined that they were learning how to fight. I learned to be a little acrobatic and how to make cool moves in the air. Put me up against someone who had trained &quot;fighting&quot; and I'd be crying and pissing myself.<br /> <br /> Now let's look at the actual Style Merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Avoidance: </b>It's completely unnecessary to have Manipulation 3 as a prerequisite for this style. If you really want Manipulation as a prerequisite at all, bring it down to 2, Athletics can remain at 2 and the Stealth 2 should be swapped for Subterfuge 1.<br /> <br /> <i>Insignificance: </i>Okay, the first technique could use Stealth because you're trying to blend in to seem non-threatening, but I'd argue that seeming non-threatening could equally well fall under Subterfuge.<br /> <br /> <i>Whack-a-Mole: </i>This technique calls out for a Manipulation + Persuasion + Avoidance roll against your enemy's attack. Once again, change it to Subterfuge. You're not <i>persuading </i>your opponent to injure themselves. You're tricking them into injuring themselves.<br /> <br /> <i>Play Dead: </i>Finally a technique that uses Subterfuge without me having to house rule it.<br /> <br /> Avoidance is a cool style, but I think I made it make more sense with my complaints above. It fits as a Subterfuge-heavy style, and should therefore require basic Subterfuge instead of Stealth 2 to learn.To have it require Manipulation 3 is just nuts.<br /> <br /> <b>Berserker: </b>This style requires Stamina 3 and Iron Stamina 3. For the theme of this particular style, it works. You have to really build a specific type of character though through the Iron Stamina requirement. But this isn't the typical fighting style.<br /> <br /> <b>Bowmanship: </b>It requires Dexterity 3, Firearms 2, Trained Observer 1. I think Dexterity 3 is steep. You don't have to be masterful to start learning these techniques. Dexterity 2 is fine. I'd argue that bowmanship isn't very dexterious in its requirement and execution at all. Composure could have been another trait that would have worked as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <b>Boxing: </b>Very jack of all trades with the requirements. It works though. I like the techniques overall. It feels like a very powerful and fun style to have in game.<br /> <br /> <b>Chain Weapons: </b>This style requires Strength 3 and Dexterity 3 which means that if you want to have it chargen, your Stamina must be 1. I hate that. My character is being railroaded into a certain way just because I want to have this particular style. Once gain, stop being to strict on the requirements. It's completely unnecessary. I'd suggest that the Strength requirement is removed completely. Dexterity can remain at 3 because of how difficult it is to control chain weapons.<br /> <br /> <b>Combat Archery: </b>It makes sense to have Strength as a requirement here because of how exerting archery is, but I'm curious why it's so completely different in its requirements than <i>Bowmanship</i>. I would change these prerequirements a little, and not necessary &quot;nerf&quot; them. They are currently Strength 3, Athletics 2, Quick Draw (Bow). I'll lower Strength 2 and add in Dexterity 2 as well. It fits better here than in <i>Bowmanship </i>(which I suggest Composure for) because of the active nature of this style.<br /> <br /> <b>Falconry: </b>It requires Wits 3 and Animal Ken 3, and you need the Bonded Condition with the bird. I'm fine with Animal Ken 3 but I question the need for Wits 3. I think Wits 2 or maybe Presence 2 would work here, but I don't care enough to actually house rule it.<br /> <br /> <b>Grappling: </b>Lower the Stamina requirement from 3 to 2. Then I'm fine with it.<br /> <br /> <b>K-9: </b>My comments on this style are the same as my comments on <i>Falconry </i>above.<br /> <br /> <b>Kino Mutai: </b>I'd suggest swapping the Dexterity requirement for Stamina. I'm fine with keeping Resolve at 3 because you're actually biting people.<br /> <br /> <b>Martial Arts: </b>The prerequirements are absolutely too high here. You can remove the Resolve requirement completely. Dexterity can be reduced to 2. Athletics and Brawl can remain as they are. If you really want to keep Resolve for some reason (you shouldn't), then lower it to 2. When comparing these tecniques to the ones in the rulebook, the rulebook are somewhat more interesting to me. I think these are solid alternatives though, and I'm fine with mixing them up.<br /> <br /> <b>Mounted Combat: </b>Lower Dexterity to 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Powered Projectile: </b>Same here. It's unnecessary to force Dexterity 3 on you to learn these techniques.<br /> <br /> <b>Spear and Bayonet: </b>Lower Strength to 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Staff Fighting: </b>Hmm. I've trained staff fighting a lot when I was a &quot;cool&quot; kid as mentioned above. Though it's not as difficult as chain weapons, it is very difficult to maintain control over the staff while in a situation where someone is fighting back. I'm fine with keeping the prerequirements as they are.<br /> <br /> <b>Strength Performance: </b>Well, since this style focuses on strength feats, I'm going to do something crazy and <i>not </i>suggest to lower that requirement.<br /> <br /> <b>Systema: </b>This is a <i>fun </i>style that I think you can play around with a lot in game. It has steep requirements, but the nature of the style justifies that it's a step above some of the other styles in its prerequisites. I'm fine with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Thrown Weapons: </b>Throwing weapons is <i>hard</i>. I'll keep the prerequisites as they are for this one. Maybe even add Composure 2 as a secondary prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <b>Two Weapon Fighting: </b>It doesn't need Wits 3 as a prerequisite. It doesn't really need Wits at all, to be honest. Change it to Dexterity 2. Keep Fighting Finesse, and keep Weaponry at 3.<br /> <br /> <b>Weapon and Shield: </b>Lower both Strength and Stamina to 2. Lower Weaponry to 1.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to comment on each of the <i>Individual Merits</i>, but I do like most of them. I especially enjoy <i>Roadkill</i>. When we were creating some characters for some of my friends, one of them wanted to play a trucker with high Drive. We debated a lot whether to get <i>Roadkill</i> and <i>Aggressive Driving</i>, both of which are Merits I've read before when we made those characters and both of which I enjoyed a lot. He decided not to get them (right now) because of the steep requirements in combination with some of the driving Merits from the rulebook he wanted instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Drone Control: </b>I don't think this style needs Intelligence 3. It probably doesn't even need Computer 3. I'd argue that you should lower both to 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>LASTING TRAUMA</b><br /> <br /> I've been thinking about how to run this. I have my solo game that I've mentioned a lot before, in which the character isn't combat oriented at all. I'd probably be very gritty when it comes to violence in that game. I am going to storytell for a group IRL too, and those have differing opinions about what makes a roleplaying game fun. Though they all have experiences with older WoD games, they like active games where they roll a lot of dice. You can certainly do that in this game, but the focus of this game is on the storytelling. I'm not sure they'd go for the gritty combat. We'll have to see how it feel in game, I suppose.<br /> <br /> There's this info box called <i>Or Death (Optional) </i>where it suggests that you can forego death and instead take on a lasting injury. When I storytell Exalted 3E, I do this, telling players that they can cheat death once per story in exchange for a crippling effect. We had this cool scene where the Twilight Caste was stabbed in the eye, and he's been wearing an eyepatch since. Now he's lost his other eye too and is going for this whole Zatoichi shtick. For a game like Exalted, that works. It's cool. The characters feel like badasses. And you can eventually let them heal their crippling injuries as the reward for an epic storyline.<br /> <br /> In this game, though. I'm not sure. I kind of like the idea of putting the fear of death in my players.<br /> <br /> I wish the new Conditions in this chapter would have been part of the Condition Cards I bought. I can probably whip something together myself though.<br /> <br /> <br /> I really wanted to finish this chapter right away, but the <i>Violent Skills </i>part is too text heavy for me to have time to invest in it right now. So we'll leave it like this for now and pick it up again later. Now I'm off for BBQ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:03:37-07:00","id":1068294,"title":"","content":"Ok, the thing about the prerequisites is that a score of two is average, so just about <i>everyone</i> has a score of 2 or more in most attributes.<br /> <br /> If you reduce all the prerequisites to two then they stop being things that guide a certain character type towards a style and just end up not mattering 90% of the time. It just loses all thematic weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:07:34-07:00","id":1068295,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so you've noticed the extremely high prerequisites. This is, oddly enough, a pretty common thing with Merits, especially in supplement books as opposed to core books, in my experience, and especially with violence-related Merits. It's cool that you have a good idea how you would adjust the prerequisites for your own game, that's a good attitude to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T10:52:44-07:00","id":1068342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068275#post1068275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;SNIP&gt;<br /> I enjoyed the paragraph about the arguments over the best style. When I was in grade school, I was a judo kid. I thought I was really cool at the time. As I became a teenager, I had watched a bunch of kung fu movies and started training hung gar kuen, tai chi and sanshou. I learned how to flail around while thinking I was cool. Then when I got older (17-18), I realized that I was bowing to altars in a dojo and talking about chi like some weird religious sect. I suddenly found the whole thing completely ridiculous and stopped doing it. But then again, I didn't train &quot;fighting&quot;. I went to a class where people imagined that they were learning how to fight. I learned to be a little acrobatic and how to make cool moves in the air. Put me up against someone who had trained &quot;fighting&quot; and I'd be crying and pissing myself.<br /> ...<br /> <b>Two Weapon Fighting: </b>It doesn't need Wits 3 as a prerequisite. It doesn't really need Wits at all, to be honest. Change it to Dexterity 2. Keep Fighting Finesse, and keep Weaponry at 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the best descriptions of pseudo-combative training I've ever heard. Learning to break a block is very different from learning how to break walls with people.<br /> <br /> As a florentine fighter, I disagree on your 'fix' for two-weapon fighting. You're not just keeping track of two weapons, it also requires an increased spatial awareness and ability to use your weapons in ways they're potentially not designed to be used. Generally speaking, two swords is for someone prepared to deal with five; one poking at you, and two broken things that chance or skill destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T14:58:36-07:00","id":1068427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068294#post1068294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, the thing about the prerequisites is that a score of two is average, so just about <i>everyone</i> has a score of 2 or more in most attributes.<br /> <br /> If you reduce all the prerequisites to two then they stop being things that guide a certain character type towards a style and just end up not mattering 90% of the time. It just loses all thematic weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>As well, while the prerequisites can seem high:<br /> <br /> 1) The vast majority of them are in traits you want to have high for a combat focused character anyway.<br /> <br /> 2) The vast majority of them are in traits that are useful on their own.<br /> <br /> 3) These are not creation only mechanics. Some Merits are better for advanced characters, and some are better for starting characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:19:00-07:00","id":1068458,"title":"","content":"I consider a lot of these merits kinda clunky in execution. I feel a certain dissonance between them and Corebook Rules, and sadly it isn't with favor for the Hurt Locker's material. It didn't feel very good on paper, and ended up feeling not very good in practice too, so currently we removed them from our material pool.<br /> <br /> The thing about violence in this game is that it's really overpriced. &quot;Sensible&quot; competent physical fighter needs a lot of redundant skill dots, often is forced to have awkward attribute dot placement at chargen, and investing into combat related merits is insanely costly due to the fact that styles need a lot of dots to &quot;click&quot; together and have a lasting impact.<br /> <br /> Which is kinda weird, because these things might not come up at all in 3 or 4 sessions (especially if you play with assumption that &quot;combat is a failure state&quot; that should be avoided), while investing into something like Status or Resources could give you plenty of benefits to use each session. <br /> Physical combatants that can't &quot;cheat&quot; by using supernatural powers to gain advantage are really kicked in the balls by the system. It's easier to be a polyglot socialite than a punchperson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-26-2017, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:25:21-07:00","id":1068460,"title":"","content":"Question for the knowledgable: Was Hurt Locker released before or after the 2nd Edition corebook?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:29:21-07:00","id":1068465,"title":"","content":"It was released just a tiny bit ago. It's a 2nd Edition Book that was released after multiple 2nd Edition Gamelines Corebooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:30:02-07:00","id":1068466,"title":"","content":"After. It actually references several things from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:40:29-07:00","id":1068470,"title":"","content":"Other thing I disliked about these materials were drawbacks in the Merits. If they were mentioned as a optional rule it would be fine, but they feel really out of place to me for the same reason why &quot;Small Framed&quot; does - they just feel incoherent with the rest of system. Ripples and dissonance, kinda like suddenly encountering alien random object inserted into the game from another game following different design principles. That, and they forcefeed you a specific &quot;character concept&quot; for given merit. Air of Menace would be fantastic for a intimidating, charismatic &quot;Mafia Boss&quot; type of character...except you are forced one specific interpretation of the &quot;so scary people are afraid to attack them&quot; making you scarred brute who is socially disadvantaged.<br /> <br /> Instead of forcing a drawback on me, maybe put in a sidebar about &quot;hey, some merits might have interesting drawbacks, if you accept them you can decrease the cost/requirement/whatever by X! Here are some examples for drawbacks, feel free to experiment with previously published merits and adding your own drawbacks to them!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Carrots, not sticks&quot;, something something. I hope this design direction will not appear again, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:57:29-07:00","id":1068476,"title":"","content":"Small-framed is a bad merit? I use it all the time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T17:04:01-07:00","id":1068478,"title":"","content":"It's bad in the sense that it's the only merit in the corebook that makes you actively worse at certain activities while taxing you full price for accompanying benefits. Again, you could model what Small Framed tries to do by leaving out it's drawback (smaller health, etc) and introducing a Persistent Condition that can be taken to &quot;do the thing&quot;.<br /> It just sticks out, for no good design reason.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Imagine that Domination Discipline suddenly has this added to it:<br /> &quot;Because you are a mindbending manipulative monster, and of course you are, why would you take this Discipline otherwise, people are afraid of you and you suffer First Impression penalties in Social Manuevering and roll penalties to Social rolls that would be at disadvantage due to fear of your character&quot;. Looks heavy handed? That's how Air of Menace and Cohesive feel to me - pretty cool generic effects that could be a nice addition to the toolbox, heavily handed forced into a specific narrative that isn't the only or best way to represent these mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-26-2017, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T17:14:22-07:00","id":1068483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068478#post1068478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's bad in the sense that it's the only merit in the corebook that makes you actively worse at certain activities while taxing you full price for accompanying benefits. Again, you could model what Small Framed tries to do by leaving out it's drawback (smaller health, etc) and introducing a Persistent Condition that can be taken to &quot;do the thing&quot;.<br /> It just sticks out, for no good design reason.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Imagine that Domination Discipline suddenly has this added to it:<br /> &quot;Because you are a mindbending manipulative monster, and of course you are, why would you take this Discipline otherwise, people are afraid of you and you suffer First Impression penalties in Social Manuevering and roll penalties to Social rolls that would be at disadvantage due to fear of your character&quot;. Looks heavy handed? That's how Air of Menace and Cohesive feel to me - pretty cool generic effects that could be a nice addition to the toolbox, heavily handed forced into a specific narrative that isn't the only or best way to represent these mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> so, would you make small-framed into something that could do it effect with a drawback based on why it works on your character? Like, you're harder to notice because you just look really abnormally average-looking. Then give a Persistent Condition modeling the social drawbacks to that. Or you're just really stealthy, but it requires years of training and maybe some equipment to acquire that version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T17:27:41-07:00","id":1068490,"title":"","content":"Yes, which would open up multiple stealthy concepts that don't have to rely on being literally small or throw dice at me for taking away their health box while still asking them to give me two of their STARTING merits, which are more valuable than XP spent on merits during the game (because there are certain things that can be bought only at char gen, or things that can be *traded for* Merit dots and often are better than Merits; thankfully, both of these seem to be slowly but steadily culled and extirpated from the game)<br /> <br /> By the way, you know what would be awesome for Hurt Locker? A big list of Persistent Conditions modeling different and interesting problems that can hover around the character and fit the theme of the book. Something like Lasting Trauma section, but expanded to include other things that aren't necessarily restricted to bodily harm or a specific supernatural template.<br /> Show me how to model being a Gang Member using a condition, show me a &quot;Stalked&quot; Condition so a *thought of playing such character* can enter my mind, give me a Condition woven with the stuff from the Menace of Air that makes my character visibly belonging to the life of violence and fear; <br /> Each such Condition could also double as a story seed, and provide a teaching tool to the buyer: &quot;here are multiple ways to write and balance an condition, analyze them with these guidelines in mind and you will amaze your players with Improvise-A-Condition routine meeting their exact needs!&quot; <br /> If there is one thing I really dislike about a lot of CofD material, it's how a lot of it is &quot;here is a cool idea seed about a mechanic or something, it's totally cool, we don't have any examples of it or any guidelines about how you can write them yourself, but don't worry, you are a big trooper, you will certainly figure something out, gotta go write something else&quot;.<br /> <br /> One of most memorable moments about my GM learning these books was a desperate, angry spontaneous outbreak of &quot;IF I WANTED TO HOMEBREW EVERYTHING WITH NO GUIDELINES TO COMPARE AND FOLLOW, I WOULDN'T BUY THIS BOOK FOR A PRICE OF A COMPLETE VIDEO GAME&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-26-2017, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T19:13:34-07:00","id":1068510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068478#post1068478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's bad in the sense that it's the only merit in the corebook that makes you actively worse at certain activities while taxing you full price for accompanying benefits. Again, you could model what Small Framed tries to do by leaving out it's drawback (smaller health, etc) and introducing a Persistent Condition that can be taken to &amp;quot;do the thing&amp;quot;.<br /> It just sticks out, for no good design reason.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Imagine that Domination Discipline suddenly has this added to it:<br /> &amp;quot;Because you are a mindbending manipulative monster, and of course you are, why would you take this Discipline otherwise, people are afraid of you and you suffer First Impression penalties in Social Manuevering and roll penalties to Social rolls that would be at disadvantage due to fear of your character&amp;quot;. Looks heavy handed? That's how Air of Menace and Cohesive feel to me - pretty cool generic effects that could be a nice addition to the toolbox, heavily handed forced into a specific narrative that isn't the only or best way to represent these mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying, but I would point out that Dominate <i>does</i> have that drawback, in the sense that you must be a vampire to have Dominate, and all vampires suffer Social penalties to interactions with humans based on their Humanity. It's just that &quot;because you're a mindbending manipulative monster, and of course you are, why would you have this Discipline otherwise&quot; isn't directly stated in so few words, but demonstrated over the course of the rest of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T19:43:46-07:00","id":1068516,"title":"","content":"Dominate doesn't have that drawback, because that drawback is a result of Humanity mechanic, which is a different part of Vampire template. It's a Low Humanity Drawback, not &quot;specific gameplay option you spend XP or chargen resources on in order to improve your character&quot; drawback. It's like saying that falling unconcious due to damage is a Prime Arcanum drawback, because Mages fall unconcious when damaged enough. <br /> <br /> Anyway, to avoid the rabbit hole of discussing if it's a Dominate drawback or Vampire drawback or Humanity drawback, replace the &quot;Domination Discipline&quot; with &quot;Mind Arcanum&quot;. Or add a line to Firefight, &quot;You are a gunfighter, which means you are a gun nut, gun nuts are scary and will shoot you to death, suffer social penalties for it!&quot;. Or add a line to Hobbyist Clique &quot;As a member of hobbyist clique, you suffer from a reputation of being a nerd, so take a social penalty and decrease your First Impression against people who don't share your hobby&quot;. Or add a line to Iron Will, &quot;Because you are so adamant in your way of thinking, you are kind of a jerkass who only cares about their own opinion, take a social penalty and decrease your First Impression against people who dislike people strongly entrenched in their opinion&quot;<br /> <br /> That's how I perceive Air of Menace.<br /> <br /> You could easily replace it with &quot;Your character is scary! Maybe they are big and imposing, or their smiles and soft words strangle you like sneaky snakes! When you call deer a horse, no one in the room objects! People with less Intimidation than you need to spend Willpower in order to take an action against you!&quot;<br /> Why ignore +2 to Intimidation rolls? Because you can already do that with Striking Looks. In fact, current Air of Menace allows you to grab both Air of Menace and Striking Looks (&quot;scary as fuck&quot;), to get +4 on Intimidation dice rolls.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T04:36:07-07:00","id":1068610,"title":"","content":"How I perceive Air of Menace is &quot;You are better at using Hard Leverage. However, you are also worse at using Soft Leverage. Oh, also people are a bit scared of you so they need to spend willpower to attack unless they are even scarier&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, there's no reason you can't use it for a scary charismatic mob boss, but if they're trying to play nice they're going to have to work a little harder. Get a good impression with prep and appeal to vices. Shouldn't be hard for a <i>Mob Boss. </i>I don't think the merit bars you from entry to that sort of character. I think it fits <i>perfectly. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T07:22:05-07:00","id":1068654,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar482_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"482\" data-vbnamecard=\"482\">Ekorren</a> interesting to see a fellow Martial Artist take a peek at this book, though I'm a little sad you got saddled with a &quot;spirituality and performance&quot; instructor who acted as if they were teaching you genuine self-defence skills. My master is very good at the demonstration and performance aspect (he likes to tell a story about how almost fifteen years ago someone wanted him to be the Red Ranger's stunt double on the then-current iteration of Power Rangers), but he's also no nonsense about about practical application, has trained with very scary people, and has no trouble bringing in those very scary people (some of whom are also very nice and laid back) in order to teach the more dedicated students some stuff, including me.<br /> <br /> I like the Fighting Style Merits section because it lets you pick and choose which maneuvers you want from a Style, which I feel is more representative of how actual martial arts works in terms of picking techniques that work for you, and also a wide variety of maneuvers that I actually <i>recognize</i> and can perform myself. What I learned from Hurt Locker is that, apparently in the CofD, I'm actually a very scary person, which I find somewhat hilarious.<br /> <br /> Probably my favourite non-fighting non-Supernatural Merit definitely has to be Object Fetishism, because it makes you not only more combat viable (Willpower is a great way to boost stats) but also because it gives you the opportunity to have mortal psychics with objects they've tied to their soul and draw on for magic. It <i>certainly </i>makes it easier to use Supernatural Merits, considering the most powerful burn through Willpower quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T12:18:50-07:00","id":1068790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068654#post1068654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar482_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"482\" data-vbnamecard=\"482\">Ekorren</a> interesting to see a fellow Martial Artist take a peek at this book, though I'm a little sad you got saddled with a &quot;spirituality and performance&quot; instructor who acted as if they were teaching you genuine self-defence skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't call me a martial artist. You don't call yourself a football player if you played some football in high school, if that's over ten years ago. My criticism is against the whole pretend-culture that martial arts dojos have going for them. I understand that they &quot;want to pay their respects to the culture and whatnot,&quot; but the fact of the matter is that the schools have a romanticized view of some make-believe martial arts culture that's about as Asian as a fortune cookie. There are basically no differences in being a member of a kung fu class and being a member of a cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 03-27-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T12:37:19-07:00","id":1068801,"title":"","content":"ok, that last comment is a bit too far. There's no love bombing, stealing all your money and making you cut all ties to anyone outside the organization. Don't dilute the evil that is cults with exaggerated comparisons with martial arts classes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T12:56:16-07:00","id":1068809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068801#post1068801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, that last comment is a bit too far. There's no love bombing, stealing all your money and making you cut all ties to anyone outside the organization. Don't dilute the evil that is cults with exaggerated comparisons with martial arts classes</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, I'm sure that not <i>all</i> cults go to those extremes. So Ekorren probably isn't completely off base here. Probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T12:58:25-07:00","id":1068810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068809#post1068809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to be fair, I'm sure that not <i>all</i> cults go to those extremes. So Ekorren probably isn't completely off base here. Probably.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's why they use &quot;new religious movement&quot; to refer to psychologically healthy cults now. There's a reason that word is an insult now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:13:40-07:00","id":1068821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068810#post1068810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's why they use <b>&quot;new religious movement&quot;</b> to refer to psychologically healthy cults now. There's a reason that word is an insult now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have literally never heard anyone anywhere refer to one as that ever, so ignoring this new politically correct re-branding, my point stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:15:08-07:00","id":1068823,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, I've been waiting to see a good Fighting Style representation of Aikido or Nihon Goshin Aikido for quite sometime. From your descriptions of &quot;Avoidance&quot; it seems like it may come close. <br /> <br /> When I studied Nihon goshin Aikido, half of my sensei were practical minded and the other half were spiritual minded but they intersected interestingly. They freely said that this art is not effective if the goal is to win a combat. So the art is more of a compliment leaving a bad situation rather than a way to neutralize one. Both aspects of it resonated with me so it would be cool to see a Fighting Style merit that is in line with the blending with/through conflict that I remember. Though it sounds like avoidance might be close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:16:07-07:00","id":1068824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068801#post1068801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, that last comment is a bit too far. There's no love bombing, stealing all your money and making you cut all ties to anyone outside the organization. Don't dilute the evil that is cults with exaggerated comparisons with martial arts classes</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of differences. I was exaggerating the comparison because of my own experiences with martial arts schools. My point remains though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T14:51:15-07:00","id":1068885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068821#post1068821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have literally never heard anyone anywhere refer to one as that ever, so ignoring this new politically correct re-branding, my point stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the heck is your criteria for cult then? I have plenty of friends who are pagan and would have been branded as being part of a &quot;cult&quot; 20 or 30 years ago. They still get called that sometimes because they live in a rural conservative area, cult herby meaning &quot;not Christian&quot; and &quot;I don't understand or like what they believe.&quot; I've heard Leliel's exact phrase used, but not calling them cultists is a basic sign of respect for their faith and beliefs, and an acknowledgement that their practices are neither harmful nor predatory. It's not rebranding, it's decent respect towards other people.<br /> <br /> (And for the record, I'm a hardcore athiest-humanist, so please no one use the &quot;all religions are cults&quot; line of reasoning with me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T14:55:30-07:00","id":1068886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068885#post1068885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What the heck is your criteria for cult then? I have plenty of friends who are pagan and would have been branded as being part of a &quot;cult&quot; 20 or 30 years ago. They still get called that sometimes because they live in a rural conservative area, cult herby meaning &quot;not Christian&quot; and &quot;I don't understand or like what they believe.&quot; I've heard Leliel's exact phrase used, but not calling them cultists is a basic sign of respect for their faith and beliefs, and an acknowledgement that their practices are neither harmful nor predatory. It's not rebranding, it's decent respect towards other people.<br /> <br /> (And for the record, I'm a hardcore athiest-humanist, so please no one use the &quot;all religions are cults&quot; line of reasoning with me.)</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Cult: a system of religious veneration and devotion directed toward a particular figure or object.</span></span><br /> <br /> And yes, all religions are also cults by definition, just larger and generally more accepted. You might not like the answer but it doesn't stop it from being true. Some people might demonize the word, but that doesn't stop it from meaning what it means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-27-2017, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:10:59-07:00","id":1068890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068886#post1068886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Cult: a system of religious veneration and devotion directed toward a particular figure or object.</span></span><br /> <br /> And yes, all religions are also cults by definition, just larger and generally more accepted. You might not like the answer but it doesn't stop it from being true. Some people might demonize the word, but that doesn't stop it from meaning what it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the same sort of logic that people use to justify the continued use of racial slurs (I don't need to list them, we know which ones I'm referring to). That's also the same argument that people use to call me and people like me retarded, despite the negative connotations that carries. Even if it is linguisticly correct, it is grossly inappropriate and disrespectful in the context of a modern religious movement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:13:57-07:00","id":1068892,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the word cult has had (and still has) several different meanings depending on region, time period and the very person you happen to discuss it with.<br /> One definition of cult is religious system. Another is deviant religious system (as in being in minority). A third one is closed religious systems that has little to no insight or possibility of induction. A fourth is the same as the third except it isn't limited to religious societies. A fifth is a closed society where participation is mandatory once you've been inducted. A sixth is any organized belief (religious, political, whatever) that is thought of being divorced from reality by the one using the term (&quot;Political party X is a cult. Why else would they even believe their policy Y could ever work?&quot;).<br /> <br /> Discussing what the word cult means is generally useless. It's better to just clarify what you meant if you happened to use the word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:17:05-07:00","id":1068893,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's not turn this into a thread about religion. I used exaggerated terms when expressing criticism against martial arts classes because I have a tendency of not being very politically correct. I did not intend to derail into something that could actually upset people, and that's what I feel a discussion about religion will undoubtedly lead to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:28:23-07:00","id":1068901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068890#post1068890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the same sort of logic that people use to justify the continued use of racial slurs (I don't need to list them, we know which ones I'm referring to). That's also the same argument that people use to call me and people like me retarded, despite the negative connotations that carries. Even if it is linguisticly correct, it is grossly inappropriate and disrespectful in the context of a modern religious movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, insults are insults. If someone is wanting to insult you then regardless of what they choose to call you their intentions are the same. And you can make anything into an insult if you use the right tone, you damn forum poster (See? Though seriously, don't somehow realistically take offense to that, it's silly and is meant to be used as an example). I know I've had this conversation on here before, though I can't quite remember with who. Long story short, you can't decide for other people how they're going to feel about what you say, so you may as well say what is technically correct as long as it isn't directly insulting someone else. Further more, when we are discussing semantics, which is what was happening here, people need to be able to take shit with a grain of salt and be able to discuss things without getting riled up over things (assuming they aren't being intentionally insulted).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068892#post1068892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the word cult has had (and still has) several different meanings depending on region, time period and the very person you happen to discuss it with.<br /> One definition of cult is religious system. Another is deviant religious system (as in being in minority). A third one is closed religious systems that has little to no insight or possibility of induction. A fourth is the same as the third except it isn't limited to religious societies. A fifth is a closed society where participation is mandatory once you've been inducted. A sixth is any organized belief (religious, political, whatever) that is thought of being divorced from reality by the one using the term (&quot;Political party X is a cult. Why else would they even believe their policy Y could ever work?&quot;).<br /> <br /> Discussing what the word cult means is generally useless. It's better to just clarify what you meant if you happened to use the word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, like most things, context matters here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068893#post1068893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, let's not turn this into a thread about religion. I used exaggerated terms when expressing criticism against martial arts classes because I have a tendency of not being very politically correct. I did not intend to derail into something that could actually upset people, and that's what I feel a discussion about religion will undoubtedly lead to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have absolutely no intention of starting a full blown conversation about religion/cultism/ideology/whatever here. It's typically a fairly useless thing to argue over imo, since most people are usually so entrenched in their belief that nothing anyone on either side says is ever going to change anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-27-2017, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:43:59-07:00","id":1068911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068901#post1068901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, insults are insults. If someone is wanting to insult you then regardless of what they choose to call you their intentions are the same. And you can make anything into an insult if you use the right tone, you damn forum poster (See? Though seriously, don't somehow realistically take offense to that, it's silly and is meant to be used as an example). I know I've had this conversation on here before, though I can't quite remember with who. Long story short, you can't decide for other people how they're going to feel about what you say, so you may as well say what is technically correct as long as it isn't directly insulting someone else. Further more, when we are discussing semantics, which is what was happening here, people need to be able to take shit with a grain of salt and be able to discuss things without getting riled up over things (assuming they aren't being intentionally insulted).</div> </div> </div> </div>And my point is that if you know something is insulting and there is another thing that is also linguistically correct, you should use that instead. If you don't know and someone says what you're saying is insulting, you should respect that and believe them. If you continue to use the same language when there are equally linguistically correct alternatives that aren't insulting in that context, you (or I or anyone, I don't intend this to be personal) are being rude at best. It is semantics, but those semantics are relevant. If someone insisted on using retard to talk about me or anyone with learning disabilities, even after I asked them not to, it would not end well. The similarity between these two uses of language are why this matters to me. Something being semantic does not mean irrelevant. <br /> <br /> I have made my point though, and I will drop it. Hopefully I'll have my thoughts on Chapter 2 up tonight or tomorrow morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:52:47-07:00","id":1068914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1068911#post1068911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And my point is that if you know something is insulting and there is another thing that is also linguistically correct, you should use that instead. If you don't know and someone says what you're saying is insulting, you should respect that and believe them. If you continue to use the same language when there are equally linguistically correct alternatives that aren't insulting in that context, you (or I or anyone, I don't intend this to be personal) are being rude at best. It is semantics, but those semantics are relevant. If someone insisted on using retard to talk about me or anyone with learning disabilities, even after I asked them not to, it would not end well. The similarity between these two uses of language are why this matters to me. Something being semantic does not mean irrelevant.<br /> <br /> I have made my point though, and I will drop it. Hopefully I'll have my thoughts on Chapter 2 up tonight or tomorrow morning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but here's the trick. I don't believe most words are, in and of themselves, insulting. Cult included. So again, context matters here. I believe that Ekorren was using the word cult in reference to the near religious like behavior a lot of martial arts institutions practice. A behavior shared by most (that I know of anyways) cults (technical definition here so mainstream religions count). Someone else took this to mean the worst kinds of cults and I pointed out that not all cults (again, technical definition) were like that, and that it probably wasn't as much of an exaggeration as he might believe assuming we're using the general term here and not talking about a specific subsection. So again, no one is directly being insulted. Some people may take offense regardless of there being no insult, but that isn't really an issue since there's bound to be someone who would take offense regardless, and this was a case of arguing semantics anyways.<br /> <br /> Though yes, I think we've both gotten as much out of this as we're going to get. So carry on everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T16:23:26-07:00","id":1068928,"title":"","content":"When I think of cults, I either think of ancient, secretive mystery cults or, more likely, the Pierre's modern scams that grind up and abuse the emotionally vulnerable. I'll leave it at that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T16:51:14-07:00","id":1068935,"title":"","content":"Out of Curiosity now, after rereading your read through of CHP. 2. What kinds of styles do you think would be welcome in the game? I know this book is all about the violence but for the purpose's of this question I'm broadening the question to more than just the violence. Like, would you want a social combat fighting style? <br /> <br /> Just trying to get ideas.<br /> <br /> (Now that i've said it I can't get the idea of a cooking style merit out of my brain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T03:32:43-07:00","id":1069228,"title":"","content":"I don't really understand why people think of social maneuvering as combat. Anyways, putting that aside...<br /> <br /> We currently have three Social Maneuvering styles - Fast Talking, Etiquette, and the currently-changeling-only-but-easy-to-convert Enchanting Performance. There's also the Pusher, Sympathetic, Empath and similar merits, which tie into the system well which create additional &quot;style merits&quot; but not formal styles.<br /> <br /> Now, I'd like to group Fast Talking and Pusher together as a kind of &quot;Con&quot; style tag. Its all about subterfuge, persuasion, bribes and appealing to one's vice.<br /> <br /> Next, we have Sympathetic and Empath. I'm tying these two together because they both key off maneuvering people through use of Empathy. You understand their pain and can relate to them better. You even take penalties to yourself (share the pain) so that you can get closer to them, and directly remove doors. There's no formal style for this, but they both key off the same idea, and it wouldn't be bad to make a full Style based off this.<br /> <br /> Air of Menance stands alone for a moment - there's no Maneuvering Style that focuses on Forcing Doors or hard leverage, really. Or, for a more general approach, one that relies on Intimidation and other implied threats. Forcing doors is pretty simplistic, so there's not a lot of room, I suppose, but I'm sure something could be done. Could even play up being intimidating on one hand, then soften up in a kind of duality that confuses people and makes them readily agree to things due to confusion, or something along those lines<br /> <br /> Etiquette is all about specializing in using Socialize. I would also include Fame, Taste and Barfly as related style tags, since those are all about blending in and having weight with specific crowds. Yes, even though Taste uses Expression and Crafts, it more relies on discussion of a specific group's interests than being more inspiring, like below.<br /> <br /> Enchanting Performance. Technically this Style is changeling only, but its easy to convert (just swap glamour for willpower). Its like a better version of the Inspiring merit for using Expression in various ways. There's not a lot that really ties into this kind of style other than being really good at Expression. I'd like to see more inspiring style merits that do more than give out Inspired, maybe tie in some persuasion for &quot;Firebranding&quot; or Cahalith style rousing. <br /> <br /> Table Turner and Closed book deserve some mention. A kind of style that turns social maneuvering back on someone for being really good at not being tricked or convinced about something.<br /> <br /> You can leverage social merits like Allies, Contacts and Status to get things done. There should be Styles that reflect using your Fame or Status or whatever appropriately. Something like a &quot;Police&quot; or other athoritarian vibe. &quot;I'm in charge, you listen to me,&quot; style. Or &quot;I know things about you&quot; type thing. Doesn't even need to be related to social maneuvering, but can mess around with other social merits and what they can leverage or produce. Or something about double-teaming with a Mentor or Retainer in social situtations. Honestly, I feel like this is a subsystem worthy of its own set of supporting abilities and expansion, just like Chase is now a second physical-based subsystem, just like Crafts.<br /> <br /> More animal-based styles of any type would be awesome. Social, combat, whatever. Animal Ken is... interesting. Its main use of rolling to training, cowing, soothing animals can really be acomplished with just one dot, same with most animal ken based magic abilities, and then just buff with specialties as necessary; much cheaper and effective that way, and often doesn't come up. Here's where animal ken shines in 2e, however. It adds to your Bonded animals' rolls. So, animal trainers that have Retainers, or perhaps Familiars / personal totems / hedgebeast companions / animal ghouls / etc can use these pets to great effect with pretty significantly large dice pools and can shrug off magic powers better than their trainers. Still, though, this is just a glorified &quot;Retainer&quot; style system like I mentioned above. At best, we can just say that we have a Style for improving the Bonded Condition. Making it apply to more diec rolls, more bonuses, having the bonus work in reverse, etc. Not exaclty social-focused, but can be used in social situations, so still relevant.<br /> <br /> At this point, we've basically covered every social skill having its own associated styles. The only one lacking at this point is Streetwise, which, to be honest, I think is more of a Mental merit than Social anyways. Hells, the write up even says its about &quot;knowlege of life on the streets. It tells her how to navigate the city, how to get information from unlikely sources, and where she\u2019ll be (relatively) safe.&quot; Its all about knowing the right things or people. My games treat it as the &quot;low&quot; version of Politics - crime versus legal, I suppose, and I would tie these two skills into that social merit thing I discussed above.<br /> <br /> Outside of linking to specific skills, I can imagine that we would have an interrogation style (police interviews, etc) for information gathering. Interrogations have Intimidate as their main skill, so perhaps that can link into Air of Menace like I talked above? The Avoidance FS, while technically a combat based merit, actually does provide a kind of good idea based on that first dot - appearing like a wallflower or similar so you can use stealth and subterfuge to be unimportant while doing other things. There could be other avenues based on that same idea. Blend in, don't pay attention to the man behind the curtain. Good for infiltration type things.<br /> <br /> That's all I got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-28-2017, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T03:44:13-07:00","id":1069232,"title":"","content":"While we're on the subject of Chapter 2 and the various Styles there.... perhaps someone can answer a question for me about the Avoidance FS? Whack-a-mole. How does one use Manipulation + Persuasion to Arm Wreck someone? Let alone as a reflexive counter attack? Seriously, I'm drawing a complete blank here. How does this work from a story perspective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T06:19:05-07:00","id":1069283,"title":"","content":"I <i>think</i> it's supposed to represent confusing and/or annoying the attacker to distracting levels and making them hurt themselves trying to hit you. Persuasion... probably isn't the best skill choice to help represent that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 03-28-2017, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T09:09:30-07:00","id":1069397,"title":"","content":"I think that the perquisites make sense for the most part, it is mentioned that you don't necessarily need these merits to perform these maneuvers so I take the merits as meaning you have the training and physical acumen to do these maneuvers reliably. I have had gruff with the strength requirements on firearms before but that's mostly focused on their definition of a heavy and light pistol. I usually don't have problems with making a good fighter at chargen, but then I'm also well known in my social circles for my ability to min-max and abuse a system to it's fullest extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T09:30:04-07:00","id":1069409,"title":"","content":"Like, over extending themselves, or something? Oh, thus the name. Try to hit a wack-a-mole that dodges out of the way and you hurt yourself swinging down too hard, I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T11:17:01-07:00","id":1069485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1069409#post1069409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, over extending themselves, or something? Oh, thus the name. Try to hit a wack-a-mole that dodges out of the way and you hurt yourself swinging down too hard, I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually is possible to hurt yourself from improperly reading distance. Usually you end up hurting an ankle or a foot or your hand though and not really something that would take you out of a fight, except for that one time a guy broke his pinkie toe on the mat when fighting me in a tournament but that was more of a fluke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T13:18:27-07:00","id":1069576,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I understand it as dodging to provoke an over extension. Somebody trying to punch you hits the concrete wall you were standing in front of, or somebody swinging an axe wrenches their shoulder with the momentum when it doesn't stop where they expected it to. Manipulation + Persuasion is sort of a strange pool to do that with, but I see what they were trying to convey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T20:01:24-07:00","id":1069806,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I would have put that as Dexterity + Subterfuge, along the lines of Cheap Shot or whatever the Street feinting merit is called. But to each their own. I'm working on making Coattails really pop through use of Parkour.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, its possible to hurt yourself, its just a very odd thing, and I'm not sure it feels right still. Feels janky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T01:29:33-07:00","id":1075791,"title":"","content":"No, I haven't given up on this yet. I had to study for the SATs, then write the SATs (I did well, by the way), then I got distracted by homebrew writing. Will try to get to this book again this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:31:43-07:00","id":1089135,"title":"","content":"Okay, after many distractions for some time now, I'm back and will keep reading this book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>CHAPTER THREE: THE OTHER SIDE</b><br /> <br /> This chapter has a lot of Supernatural Merits. I'll read them all but I may not comment on them all. There's an info box that suggests that you need to be a human to learn Supernatural Merits to avoid unnecessary complexity.<br /> <br /> I do have a few favorites immediately. I can see myself using <i>Assertive Implement</i> and <i>Bless Amulet </i>among others for a shaman type character. I picture something like a story set in the mountains of Nepal with a ghost hunter using the bound ghosts of his ancestors. Or maybe it's tied to some voodoo shenanigans. Either way, I like when you can build an entire character around something as seemingly simple as a Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Camera Obscura: </b>Fatal Frame!!!<br /> <br /> Consecrate Weapon + Assertive Implement = Even cooler character.<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Passenger: </b>This is just creepy. I thought it would be a reference to Jeff Lindsay's Dexter series.<br /> <br /> <b>Evil Eye: </b>This seems powerful for two dots. Though I'm not sure what the Insensate Tilt does so I may be wrong.<br /> <br /> <b>Fated Ferocity: </b>This was interesting. Very badass fighting style too. I like it a lot.<br /> <br /> <b>Hidden Variable: </b>I may want to use this for a later Vampire character in my game. Would something break if I let a Vampire have this?<br /> <br /> <b>Pyschokinetic Combat: </b>There are so many psychokinetic Merits in this game that I wonder how it'd be like to face someone with all of them. I probably wouldn't allow a PC to have these Merits for any type of game I'm interested in Storytelling, but I will definitely use these tools for NPCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>SUPERNATURAL MERIT TEMPLATES</b><br /> <br /> This part of the chapter presents character templates that let you play supernatural characters that are somewhere in between humans and supernatural splats. The Merit <i>Supernatural Resistance </i>helps make the character comparable to other characters that may be other splats. I wish these templates had been in the corebook, to be honest. If I would be designing a revised corebook, I'd probably keep most of the God-Machine Chronicle separate and instead add a bunch of content from Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> <b>Atariya: </b>Introduces the <i>Damn Lucky </i>Merit that's a super powerful defensive Merit that lets you ignore damage based on your Merit rating. The Merit <i>Mr. Lucky </i>works kind of like a guardian angel. This one was really interesting to me. You could play campaigns based around the mysterious Mr. Lucky. The Merit <i>Nine Lives </i>keeps you from dying, and the Merit <i>Count Down </i>lets the character know all the times she's escaped death. There are more Merits as well, all very interesting and thematic to the template. Though it says that you must be an Atariya to learn them, I suppose you could technically borrow here and there for a character without having to follow the template as written. Mr. Lucky in particular is something I could see myself using for other characters.<br /> <br /> <b>The Infected: </b>When I was generating characters together with my players, one of them expressed interest in wanting to play a character who was suffering from an untreatable form of cancer. I wasn't aware of this template at the time and I shrugged it off as something that could be addressed in game without actually needing any specific Merits for it. Now in hindsight, that character concept could have worked well as an Infected.<br /> <br /> <b>The Plain: </b>Umm ... okay.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lost Boys: </b>This was really cool. I could see myself making a game based on these guys.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychic Vampires: </b>Right. They are cool and all, but I'm pretty sure we've got some real vampires annoyed by their name choice. I know the book doesn't want me to do this, but I wonder if it would be fun to play a psychic vampire vampire. Are there such a thing as liches in the Chronicles of Darkness? I kind of want to call these guys <i>liches</i> instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> I started off with a short post now because I don't have time to read anymore at the moment. I'll try to get the post about the Tokyo chapter in as soon as possible. I'm determined to finish this book soon so that I can get started with Vampire. I'm going to need that one soon. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:52:19-07:00","id":1089190,"title":"","content":"Re: Liches - the term is used in Mage to refer to Mages who use (usually unscrupulous) magic to live forever. That said, as you continue to read CofD books, you'll find that there is a <i>lot</i> of terminology overlap. There are at least three different things called demons, for example, and potentially a lot more depending on how you count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:59:28-07:00","id":1089195,"title":"","content":"Heh. Goetic demons actually got renamed to Goetia to reduce the number of types of demons. Now we only have infernal, supernal and unchained demons, that I know of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:14:10-07:00","id":1089238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1089195#post1089195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. Goetic demons actually got renamed to Goetia to reduce the number of types of demons. Now we only have infernal, supernal and unchained demons, that I know of.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I say depending on how you count. Strix have been called demons before too, and the Lucifuge are descended from demons that may or may not be any of the ones we're familiar with, but I don't count either.<br /> <br /> 2e has cleaned this up in some ways (see goetic demon changing to goetia), and made it worse in others (don't get me started on &quot;Reach/Reaching&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:36:37-07:00","id":1089248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1089238#post1089238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I say depending on how you count. Strix have been called demons before too, and the Lucifuge are descended from demons that may or may not be any of the ones we're familiar with, but I don't count either.<br /> <br /> 2e has cleaned this up in some ways (see goetic demon changing to goetia), and made it worse in others (don't get me started on &amp;quot;Reach/Reaching&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>So have GM angels as well. Some Hunters call them &quot;Structural Demons.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:39:13-07:00","id":1089251,"title":"","content":"Since you liked the Lost Boys micro-template, you might want to keep an eye on &quot;Deviant: the Renegades&quot;, which is the next new line. It's only in the earliest, <i>earliest</i> stages right now (the core isn't even at a proper first draft stage yet, so all we know so far is what's been teased on the official thread), but it draws <i>hard</i> on many of the same themes. By the sound of it, those in the know might even mistake (or recognize?) the Lost Boys as Deviants of sorts themselves...<br /> <br /> As for psychic vampires? Well, without getting too into detail on Requiem, some of the &quot;real&quot; vampires might be annoyed by the epithet, but others might see them as weird, extremely distant family. Or given how they feed, might keep them at a distance for fear of... well, you'll see when you get there. It should probably vary wildly from vampire to vampire and region to region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:46:24-07:00","id":1089392,"title":"","content":"Yeah, one of the things about requiem is that the kindred may actually be five (or possibly just four) different things that all work in a similar way. They're totally open to other, weirder variants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:49:47-07:00","id":1089394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065343-okay-so-let-s-read-this-thing-hurt-locker?p=1089392#post1089392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, one of the things about requiem is that the kindred may actually be five (or possibly just four) different things that all work in a similar way. They're totally open to other, weirder variants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, spoilers, man! (I kid) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}